er. The Royal Corona is the everyday Bolívar — for those whose \'everyday\' means full body without exception. نكهات:  dark wood, undergrowth, black توابل.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Royal Corona\"]}, {\"name\": \"Coronas Gigantes\", \"color\": \"#4A235A\", \"story\": \"Double Corona (42 x 178mm). The longest Bolívar format — 90 دقيقة that travel through all the house\'s aromatic registers. Rare, barely distributed, sought by European الجامعون. The third hour of a Corona Gigantes is a journey in itself.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Coronas Gigantes\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Che Guevara\", \"anecdote\": \"Guevara, who generally preferred bold Cuban cigars, was known to alternate between Cohiba and Bolívar depending on his mood. \'Bolívar is for when you have something to solve,\' he reportedly said.\"}, {\"name\": \"Jean-Paul Sartre\", \"anecdote\": \"The French existentialist, who became a cigar smoker after years with a pipe, discovered Bolívar during his visits to Cuba in the 1960s and described them as \'the only absolutely honest thing in this world.\'\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Che Guevara\", \"anecdote\": \"Guevara, who generally preferred bold Cuban cigars, was known to alternate between Cohiba and Bolívar depending on his mood. \'Bolívar is for when you have something to solve,\' he supuestamente said.\"}, {\"name\": \"Jean-Paul Sartre\", \"anecdote\": \"The French existentialist, who became a cigar smoker after years with a pipe, discovered Bolívar during his visits to Cuba in the 1960s and described them as \'the only absolutely honest thing in this world.\'\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Che Guevara\", \"anecdote\": \"Guevara, who generally preferred bold Cuban cigars, was known to alternate between Cohiba and Bolívar depending on his mood. \'Bolívar is for when you have something to solve,\' he angeblich said.\"}, {\"name\": \"Jean-Paul Sartre\", \"anecdote\": \"The French existentialist, who became a cigar smoker after years with a pipe, discovered Bolívar during his visits to Cuba in the 1960s and described them as \'the only absolutely honest thing in this world.\'\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Che Guevara\", \"anecdote\": \"Guevara, who generally preferred bold Cuban cigars, was known to alternate between Cohiba and Bolívar depending on his mood. \'Bolívar is for when you have something to solve,\' he 据报道 said.\"}, {\"name\": \"Jean-Paul Sartre\", \"anecdote\": \"The French existentialist, who became a cigar smoker after years with a pipe, discovered Bolívar during his visits to Cuba in the 1960s and described them as \'the only absolutely honest thing in this world.\'\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Che Guevara\", \"anecdote\": \"Guevara, who generally preferred bold Cuban cigars, was known to alternate between Cohiba and Bolívar depending on his mood. \'Bolívar is for when you have something to solve,\' he يُقال إن said.\"}, {\"name\": \"Jean-Paul Sartre\", \"anecdote\": \"The French existentialist, who became a cigar smoker after years with a pipe, discovered Bolívar during his visits to Cuba in the 1960s and described them as \'the only absolutely honest thing in this world.\'\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Spirits\", \"name\": \"Artisanal Oaxacan Mezcal\", \"notes\": \"The smoke and earth of mezcal resonate with the telluric profile of Bolívar. A bold pairing for seasoned smokers.\"}, {\"type\": \"Coffee\", \"name\": \"Ethiopian natural process coffee\", \"notes\": \"The fruity and fermented notes of a natural process coffee temper the raw power of Bolívar. An unexpected and remarkable pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"Beer\", \"name\": \"Imperial Stout 12%\", \"notes\": \"The intensity of an imperial stout is one of the few beverages that can stand up to a Belicosos Finos. A winter pairing par excellence.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\": \"Licores\", \"name\": \"Artisanal Oaxacan Mezcal\", \"notes\": \"The smoke and earth of mezcal resonate with the telluric profile of Bolívar. A bold pairing for seasoned smokers.\"}, {\"type\": \"Café\", \"name\": \"Ethiopian natural process coffee\", \"notes\": \"The fruity and fermented notas de a natural process coffee temper the raw power of Bolívar. An unexpected and remarkable pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"Cerveza\", \"name\": \"Imperial Stout 12%\", \"notes\": \"The intensity of an imperial stout is one of the few beverages that can stand up to a Belicosos Finos. A winter pairing par excellence.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\": \"Spirituosen\", \"name\": \"Artisanal Oaxacan Mezcal\", \"notes\": \"The smoke and earth of mezcal resonate with the telluric profile of Bolívar. A bold pairing for seasoned smokers.\"}, {\"type\": \"Kaffee\", \"name\": \"Ethiopian natural process coffee\", \"notes\": \"The fruity and fermented Noten von a natural process coffee temper the raw power of Bolívar. An unexpected and remarkable pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"Bier\", \"name\": \"Imperial Stout 12%\", \"notes\": \"The intensity of an imperial stout is one of the few beverages that can stand up to a Belicosos Finos. A winter pairing par excellence.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\": \"烈酒\", \"name\": \"Artisanal Oaxacan Mezcal\", \"notes\": \"The smoke and earth of mezcal resonate with the telluric profile of Bolívar. A bold pairing for seasoned smokers.\"}, {\"type\": \"咖啡\", \"name\": \"Ethiopian natural process coffee\", \"notes\": \"The fruity and fermented 风味： a natural process coffee temper the raw power of Bolívar. An unexpected and remarkable pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"啤酒\", \"name\": \"Imperial Stout 12%\", \"notes\": \"The intensity of an imperial stout is one of the few beverages that can stand up to a Belicosos Finos. A winter pairing par excellence.\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\": \"المسكرات\", \"name\": \"Artisanal Oaxacan Mezcal\", \"notes\": \"The smoke and earth of mezcal resonate with the telluric profile of Bolívar. A bold pairing for seasoned smokers.\"}, {\"type\": \"القهوة\", \"name\": \"Ethiopian natural process coffee\", \"notes\": \"The fruity and fermented نكهات: a natural process coffee temper the raw power of Bolívar. An unexpected and remarkable pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"البيرة\", \"name\": \"Imperial Stout 12%\", \"notes\": \"The intensity of an imperial stout is one of the few beverages that can stand up to a Belicosos Finos. A winter pairing par excellence.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Bolivar';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'The specific commercial insight that created Café Crème was simple and proved durable: millions of Europeans who would never smoke a cigar would happily smoke something that looked and smelled like coffee. Henri Wintermans, who had built his Eersel factory into a reliable supplier of conventional small cigars for the Dutch market by the 1950s, recognized in the growing café culture of postwar Western Europe a potential audience that the traditional cigar trade was not serving and could not have imagined serving.\r\n\r\nThe product that resulted in 1958 was technically a cigarillo — a small, machine-made roll using Indonesian Sumatra wrapper over a blend of Java and Sumatra filler tobaccos, with a mild coffee-extract casing applied during the manufacturing process. The casing contributed an immediate aromatic identifier that the wrapper\'s mild sweetness amplified. The overall character was nothing like a serious premium cigar: no earth, no pepper, no leather, no intensity of any kind. It was gentle, consistent, slightly sweet, and unmistakably pleasant in the context of a coffee served at a French zinc bar counter or an Italian espresso machine.\r\n\r\nThe distribution strategy matched the concept precisely. Wintermans did not target tobacconists or cigar shops — he targeted cafes, brasseries, restaurants, and hotel bars. The small yellow metal box was designed to sit next to the cash register in the same visual register as a box of matches or a packet of breath mints: impulse purchase territory, not considered acquisition. The price point reinforced this positioning: Café Crème cost less than a glass of wine, making the after-dinner ritual accessible to customers who would never spend money in a tobacconist.\r\n\r\nBritish American Tobacco acquired the Wintermans business in the early 1970s, bringing corporate distribution infrastructure to a product that had already achieved remarkable penetration through the founder\'s regional networks. BAT\'s global reach extended Café Crème into markets across Africa, Asia, and the Middle East where the café culture context translated effectively.', `history_es` = 'Henri Wintermans fundó en 1904 en los Países Bajos su fábrica de cigarros y cigarillos. El Café Crème, creado en 1958, es su creación más famosa — un mini cigarro aromatizado al café con tabaco indonesio de Java y Sumatra. En los años 70 y 80 estaba presente en cada bar, cafetería y restaurante de Europa occidental.', `history_de` = 'Henri Wintermans gründete 1904 in den Niederlanden seine Zigaren- und Zigarillofabrik. Das Café Crème, 1958 kreiert, ist seine bekannteste Schöpfung — ein mini Zigarillo mit Kaffeearoma und indonesischem Tabak aus Java und Sumatra. In den 70er und 80er Jahren war es in jedem Bar, Café und Restaurant Westeuropas präsent.', `history_zh` = '亨利·温特曼斯于1904年在荷兰创立了雪茄和小雪茄工厂。1958年创造的咖啡奶油是其最著名的作品——一款带咖啡香气、使用爪哇和苏门答腊印尼烟草的迷你小雪茄。在70和80年代，它出现在西欧每一家酒吧、咖啡馆和餐厅里。', `history_ar` = 'أسّس هنري وينترمانس عام 1904 في هولندا مصنعه للسيجار والسيجاريلو. الكافيه كريم، المبتكَر عام 1958، أشهر إبداعاته — سيجاريلو صغير بعطر القهوة وتبغ إندونيسي من جاوة وسومطرة. في السبعينيات والثمانينيات كان حاضرًا في كل بار ومقهى ومطعم في أوروبا الغربية.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Café Crème Original\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The original product — coffee aroma over Java-Sumatra tobacco. Mini format (34 x 100mm), 10 minutes. Notes of flavored coffee, soft tobacco, light sweetness. The cigar your grandfather smoked after Sunday lunch. Timeless, accessible, universal.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Original\", \"Tubes\"]}, {\"name\": \"Café Crème Blue\", \"color\": \"#003399\", \"story\": \"Menthol version — mint aroma over Java tobacco. For smokers seeking freshness. Less traditional than the Original but regularly in the top 3 of European flavored cigarillo sales.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Blue\", \"Tubes Blue\"]}, {\"name\": \"Café Crème Arome\", \"color\": \"#C04000\", \"story\": \"Various flavored versions — vanilla, hazelnut, amaretto. The festive range for enthusiasts who like changing profiles with their mood. Same format and duration as the Original.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Vanille\", \"Noisette\", \"Amaretto\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Café Crème Original\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The original product — café aroma over Java-Sumatra tobacco. Mini format (34 x 100mm), 10 minutes. Notas de flavored café, soft tobacco, light sweetness. The cigar your grandfather smoked after Sunday lunch. Timeless, accessible, universal.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Original\", \"Tubes\"]}, {\"name\": \"Café Crème Blue\", \"color\": \"#003399\", \"story\": \"Menthol version — mint aroma over Java tobacco. For smokers seeking freshness. Less traditional than the Original but regularly in the top 3 of European flavored cigarillo sales.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Blue\", \"Tubes Blue\"]}, {\"name\": \"Café Crème Arome\", \"color\": \"#C04000\", \"story\": \"Various flavored versions — vainilla, avellana, amaretto. The festive range for aficionados who like changing profiles with their mood. Same format and duration as the Original.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Vanille\", \"Noisette\", \"Amaretto\"]}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Café Crème Original\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The original product — Kaffee aroma over Java-Sumatra tobacco. Mini format (34 x 100mm), 10 minutes. Noten von flavored Kaffee, soft tobacco, light sweetness. The cigar your grandfather smoked after Sunday lunch. Timeless, accessible, universal.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Original\", \"Tubes\"]}, {\"name\": \"Café Crème Blue\", \"color\": \"#003399\", \"story\": \"Menthol version — mint aroma over Java tobacco. For smokers seeking freshness. Less traditional than the Original but regularly in the top 3 of European flavored cigarillo sales.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Blue\", \"Tubes Blue\"]}, {\"name\": \"Café Crème Arome\", \"color\": \"#C04000\", \"story\": \"Various flavored versions — Vanille, Haselnuss, amaretto. The festive range for enthusiasts who like changing profiles with their mood. Same format and duration as the Original.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Vanille\", \"Noisette\", \"Amaretto\"]}]', `gamme_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Café Crème Original\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The original product — 咖啡 aroma over Java-Sumatra tobacco. Mini format (34 x 100mm), 10 分钟. 风味： flavored 咖啡, soft tobacco, light sweetness. The cigar your grandfather smoked after Sunday lunch. Timeless, accessible, universal.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Original\", \"Tubes\"]}, {\"name\": \"Café Crème Blue\", \"color\": \"#003399\", \"story\": \"Menthol version — mint aroma over Java tobacco. For smokers seeking freshness. Less traditional than the Original but regularly in the top 3 of European flavored cigarillo sales.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Blue\", \"Tubes Blue\"]}, {\"name\": \"Café Crème Arome\", \"color\": \"#C04000\", \"story\": \"Various flavored versions — 香草, 榛子, amaretto. The festive range for 爱好者 who like changing profiles with their mood. Same format and duration as the Original.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Vanille\", \"Noisette\", \"Amaretto\"]}]', `gamme_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Café Crème Original\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The original product — قهوة aroma over Java-Sumatra tobacco. Mini format (34 x 100mm), 10 دقيقة. نكهات:  flavored قهوة, soft tobacco, light sweetness. The cigar your grandfather smoked after Sunday lunch. Timeless, accessible, universal.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Original\", \"Tubes\"]}, {\"name\": \"Café Crème Blue\", \"color\": \"#003399\", \"story\": \"Menthol version — mint aroma over Java tobacco. For smokers seeking freshness. Less traditional than the Original but regularly in the top 3 of European flavored cigarillo sales.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Blue\", \"Tubes Blue\"]}, {\"name\": \"Café Crème Arome\", \"color\": \"#C04000\", \"story\": \"Various flavored versions — فانيليا, بندق, amaretto. The festive range for المتحمسون who like changing profiles with their mood. Same format and duration as the Original.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Indonesian Java\", \"vitolas\": [\"Vanille\", \"Noisette\", \"Amaretto\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"The European Café\", \"anecdote\": \"Café Crème equipped European bar counters for 40 years. In the 1980s, not offering Café Crème in a Paris or Brussels café was a commercial anomaly. This cigar introduced more Europeans to tobacco than any premium brand.\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\": \"The European Café\", \"anecdote\": \"Café Crème equipped European bar counters for 40 years. In the 1980s, not offering Café Crème in a Paris or Brussels café was a commercial anomaly. This cigar introduced more Europeans to tobacco than any premium brand.\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\": \"The European Café\", \"anecdote\": \"Café Crème equipped European bar counters for 40 years. In the 1980s, not offering Café Crème in a Paris or Brussels café was a commercial anomaly. This cigar introduced more Europeans to tobacco than any premium brand.\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"The European Café\", \"anecdote\": \"Café Crème equipped European bar counters for 40 years. In the 1980s, not offering Café Crème in a Paris or Brussels café was a commercial anomaly. This cigar introduced more Europeans to tobacco than any premium brand.\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"The European Café\", \"anecdote\": \"Café Crème equipped European bar counters for 40 years. In the 1980s, not offering Café Crème in a Paris or Brussels café was a commercial anomaly. This cigar introduced more Europeans to tobacco than any premium brand.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Coffee\", \"name\": \"Filter coffee\", \"notes\": \"The original and obvious pairing — Henri Wintermans created Café Crème to be smoked with a coffee. An immutable tradition since 1958.\"}, {\"type\": \"Cognac\", \"name\": \"VS Cognac\", \"notes\": \"The European bistro pairing — a small cognac and a Café Crème after lunch. A tradition from Bordeaux to Strasbourg.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\": \"Café\", \"name\": \"Filter coffee\", \"notes\": \"The original and obvious pairing — Henri Wintermans created Café Crème to be smoked with a coffee. An immutable tradition since 1958.\"}, {\"type\": \"Cognac\", \"name\": \"VS Cognac\", \"notes\": \"The European bistro pairing — a small cognac and a Café Crème after lunch. A tradition from Bordeaux to Strasbourg.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\": \"Kaffee\", \"name\": \"Filter coffee\", \"notes\": \"The original and obvious pairing — Henri Wintermans created Café Crème to be smoked with a coffee. An immutable tradition since 1958.\"}, {\"type\": \"Cognac\", \"name\": \"VS Cognac\", \"notes\": \"The European bistro pairing — a small cognac and a Café Crème after lunch. A tradition from Bordeaux to Strasbourg.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\": \"咖啡\", \"name\": \"Filter coffee\", \"notes\": \"The original and obvious pairing — Henri Wintermans created Café Crème to be smoked with a coffee. An immutable tradition since 1958.\"}, {\"type\": \"Cognac\", \"name\": \"VS Cognac\", \"notes\": \"The European bistro pairing — a small cognac and a Café Crème after lunch. A tradition from Bordeaux to Strasbourg.\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\": \"القهوة\", \"name\": \"Filter coffee\", \"notes\": \"The original and obvious pairing — Henri Wintermans created Café Crème to be smoked with a coffee. An immutable tradition since 1958.\"}, {\"type\": \"Cognac\", \"name\": \"VS Cognac\", \"notes\": \"The European bistro pairing — a small cognac and a Café Crème after lunch. A tradition from Bordeaux to Strasbourg.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Café Crème';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'The Camacho family grew corojo tobacco in Cuba\'s Vuelta Abajo region for generations — not any tobacco, but specifically the corojo varietal whose leaves provide the wrappers that gave Havana\'s great cigars their visual and aromatic signature. Dark, oily, consistently textured, Cuban corojo wrapper was the standard against which every other wrapper tobacco was measured. Growing it was a specialized craft, and the Camachos were among its most accomplished practitioners.\r\n\r\nThe Cuban revolution ended that chapter in 1959. Simon Camacho\'s departure from Havana was the departure of a man carrying his professional identity in seed form — literally, in the case of the corojo plants whose genetics he transported first to Miami and eventually to Honduras. The Jamastran Valley in Honduras\' Olancho Department proved to be the most promising available site: volcanic soils, altitude, and humidity patterns that experienced tobacologists recognized as potentially capable of supporting corojo cultivation.\r\n\r\nThe Honduras corojo that the Camacho family developed over the following decades is not the same plant as Cuban corojo. The terroir is genuinely different — the soil composition, the water, the microbial environment of the fermentation rooms. What resulted was a varietal that shared the visual characteristics and structural quality of the Cuban original while developing its own aromatic profile: fuller-bodied, more pepper-dominant, with an earthiness that Honduran soil imparted rather than Cuban. Several serious tasters have described it as a more extreme version of the Cuban original rather than an approximation.\r\n\r\nThe Davidoff group\'s acquisition in 2008 provided the manufacturing and distribution resources that allowed Camacho\'s transition from specialist manufacturer to international brand. The repositioning around the \'Cigars Gone Loud\' identity was commercially calculated but not inaccurate — Camacho occupies a specific register of intensity and directness that no other major brand in the Davidoff portfolio addresses. The packaging design, the range names, the overall aesthetic of deliberate aggression describe the cigars honestly: these are not subtlety exercises.', `history_es` = 'La familia Camacho cultivaba tabaco corojo en la región cubana de Vuelta Abajo. Tras la revolución, Simon Camacho transportó sus semillas de corojo a Honduras, donde las condiciones climáticas del Valle de Jamastran más se asemejaban a su terroir natal. Este trasplante creó el \'Corojo Hondureño\' — poderoso y complejo. Adquirida por Davidoff en 2008.', `history_de` = 'Die Familie Camacho baute Corojo-Tabak in Kubas Vuelta-Abajo-Region an. Nach der Revolution transportierte Simon Camacho seine Corojo-Samen nach Honduras, wo die klimatischen Bedingungen des Jamastran-Tals seinem Heimatterroir am nächsten kamen. Dieser Verpflanzung schuf den \'Honduranischen Corojo\' — kraftvoll und komplex. 2008 von Davidoff übernommen.', `history_zh` = '卡马乔家族在古巴布埃尔塔阿巴霍地区种植科罗霍烟草。革命后，西蒙·卡马乔将科罗霍种子带到洪都拉斯，那里哈马斯特兰谷的气候条件最接近他的故乡风土。这次移植创造了\'洪都拉斯科罗霍\'——强劲而复杂。2008年被大卫杜夫收购。', `history_ar` = 'زرعت عائلة كاماتشو تبغ الكوروخو في منطقة فويلتا أباخو الكوبية. بعد الثورة، نقل سيمون كاماتشو بذور الكوروخو إلى هندوراس حيث الظروف المناخية لوادي خاماستران أقرب ما تكون لتربته الأصلية. هذا الزرع خلق \'الكوروخو الهندوراسي\' — القوي والمعقد. استُحوِذ عليها ديفيدوف عام 2008.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Camacho Corojo\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"The original product — Honduran corojo wrapper over Jamastran ligero blend. Intense full body. Notes of red pepper, strong coffee, dark undergrowth. The Camacho Corojo is the world reference of \'Honduran Corojo\' — a terroir in its own right, different from the Cuban but totally legitimate.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Corojo\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Figurado\", \"Gordo\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 94, \"year\": 2019}]}, {\"name\": \"BXP\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"\'Box Pressed Xtreme\' — square pressed format, maximum power. Honduran oscuro wrapper over pure ligero. Notes of burned coffee, pure cocoa, black licorice. The BXP is the cigar Camacho proposes when it wants to show how far it can go in intensity. Seasoned smokers only.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro BXP\", \"Robusto BXP\"]}, {\"name\": \"American Barrel-Aged\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Nicaraguan-Honduran blend aged in American bourbon barrels before rolling. Notes of bourbon, toasted oak vanilla, soft spices. Medium-Full. The range proving Camacho can be complex without being brutal. The accessible exception in a catalog of warriors.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Camacho Corojo\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"The original product — Honduran corojo wrapper over Jamastran ligero blend. Intense full body. Notas de red pimienta, strong café, dark undergrowth. The Camacho Corojo is the world reference of \'Honduran Corojo\' — a terroir in its own right, different from the Cuban but totally legitimate.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Corojo\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Figurado\", \"Gordo\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 94, \"year\": 2019}]}, {\"name\": \"BXP\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"\'Box Pressed Xtreme\' — square pressed format, maximum power. Honduran oscuro wrapper over pure ligero. Notas de burned café, pure cocoa, black regaliz. The BXP is the cigar Camacho proposes when it wants to show how far it can go in intensity. Seasoned smokers only.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro BXP\", \"Robusto BXP\"]}, {\"name\": \"American Barrel-Aged\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Nicaraguan-Honduran blend aged in American bourbon barrels before rolling. Notas de bourbon, tostado oak vainilla, soft especias. Medium-Full. The range proving Camacho can be complex without being brutal. The accessible exception in a catalog of warriors.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Camacho Corojo\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"The original product — Honduran corojo wrapper over Jamastran ligero blend. Intense full body. Noten von red Pfeffer, strong Kaffee, dark undergrowth. The Camacho Corojo is the world reference of \'Honduran Corojo\' — a terroir in its own right, different from the Cuban but totally legitimate.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Corojo\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Figurado\", \"Gordo\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 94, \"year\": 2019}]}, {\"name\": \"BXP\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"\'Box Pressed Xtreme\' — square pressed format, maximum power. Honduran oscuro wrapper over pure ligero. Noten von burned Kaffee, pure cocoa, black licorice. The BXP is the cigar Camacho proposes when it wants to show how far it can go in intensity. Seasoned smokers only.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro BXP\", \"Robusto BXP\"]}, {\"name\": \"American Barrel-Aged\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Nicaraguan-Honduran blend aged in American bourbon barrels before rolling. Noten von bourbon, geröstet oak Vanille, soft Gewürze. Medium-Full. The range proving Camacho can be complex without being brutal. The accessible exception in a catalog of warriors.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Camacho Corojo\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"The original product — Honduran corojo wrapper over Jamastran ligero blend. Intense full body. 风味： red 胡椒, strong 咖啡, dark undergrowth. The Camacho Corojo is the world reference of \'Honduran Corojo\' — a terroir in its own right, different from the Cuban but totally legitimate.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Corojo\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Figurado\", \"Gordo\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 94, \"year\": 2019}]}, {\"name\": \"BXP\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"\'Box Pressed Xtreme\' — square pressed format, maximum power. Honduran oscuro wrapper over pure ligero. 风味： burned 咖啡, pure cocoa, black 甘草. The BXP is the cigar Camacho proposes when it wants to show how far it can go in intensity. Seasoned smokers only.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro BXP\", \"Robusto BXP\"]}, {\"name\": \"American Barrel-Aged\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Nicaraguan-Honduran blend aged in American bourbon barrels before rolling. 风味： bourbon, 烘烤 oak 香草, soft 香料. Medium-Full. The range proving Camacho can be complex without being brutal. The accessible exception in a catalog of warriors.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Camacho Corojo\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"The original product — Honduran corojo wrapper over Jamastran ligero blend. Intense full body. نكهات:  red فلفل, strong قهوة, dark undergrowth. The Camacho Corojo is the world reference of \'Honduran Corojo\' — a terroir in its own right, different from the Cuban but totally legitimate.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Corojo\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Figurado\", \"Gordo\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 94, \"year\": 2019}]}, {\"name\": \"BXP\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"\'Box Pressed Xtreme\' — square pressed format, maximum power. Honduran oscuro wrapper over pure ligero. نكهات:  burned قهوة, pure cocoa, black عرق السوس. The BXP is the cigar Camacho proposes when it wants to show how far it can go in intensity. Seasoned smokers only.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro BXP\", \"Robusto BXP\"]}, {\"name\": \"American Barrel-Aged\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Nicaraguan-Honduran blend aged in American bourbon barrels before rolling. نكهات:  bourbon, محمَّص oak فانيليا, soft توابل. Medium-Full. The range proving Camacho can be complex without being brutal. The accessible exception in a catalog of warriors.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Simon Camacho\", \"anecdote\": \"Camacho transported his corojo tobacco seeds in his luggage from Cuba. This act — saving the seeds rather than money or jewels — has become one of the founding narratives of the Cuban cigar exile diaspora in Central America.\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Simon Camacho\", \"anecdote\": \"Camacho transported his corojo tobacco seeds in his luggage from Cuba. This act — saving the seeds rather than money or jewels — has become one of the founding narratives of the Cuban cigar exile diaspora in Central America.\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Simon Camacho\", \"anecdote\": \"Camacho transported his corojo tobacco seeds in his luggage from Cuba. This act — saving the seeds rather than money or jewels — has become one of the founding narratives of the Cuban cigar exile diaspora in Central America.\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Simon Camacho\", \"anecdote\": \"Camacho transported his corojo tobacco seeds in his luggage from Cuba. This act — saving the seeds rather than money or jewels — has become one of the founding narratives of the Cuban cigar exile diaspora in Central America.\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Simon Camacho\", \"anecdote\": \"Camacho transported his corojo tobacco seeds in his luggage from Cuba. This act — saving the seeds rather than money or jewels — has become one of the founding narratives of the Cuban cigar exile diaspora in Central America.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Bourbon\", \"name\": \"Bulleit Bourbon\", \"notes\": \"The rye-spiced, dry bourbon pairs naturally with Honduran Corojo. Shared pepper notes in both.\"}, {\"type\": \"Beer\", \"name\": \"Artisan porter\", \"notes\": \"The chocolaty depth of an American porter complements the burned coffee notes of the Camacho Corojo.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\": \"Bourbon\", \"name\": \"Bulleit Bourbon\", \"notes\": \"The rye-spiced, dry bourbon pairs naturally with Honduran Corojo. Shared pepper notes in both.\"}, {\"type\": \"Cerveza\", \"name\": \"Artisan porter\", \"notes\": \"The chocolaty depth of an American porter complements the burned coffee notas de the Camacho Corojo.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\": \"Bourbon\", \"name\": \"Bulleit Bourbon\", \"notes\": \"The rye-spiced, dry bourbon pairs naturally with Honduran Corojo. Shared pepper notes in both.\"}, {\"type\": \"Bier\", \"name\": \"Artisan porter\", \"notes\": \"The chocolaty depth of an American porter complements the burned coffee Noten von the Camacho Corojo.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\": \"波旁威士忌\", \"name\": \"Bulleit Bourbon\", \"notes\": \"The rye-spiced, dry bourbon pairs naturally with Honduran Corojo. Shared pepper notes in both.\"}, {\"type\": \"啤酒\", \"name\": \"Artisan porter\", \"notes\": \"The chocolaty depth of an American porter complements the burned coffee 风味： the Camacho Corojo.\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\": \"البوربون\", \"name\": \"Bulleit Bourbon\", \"notes\": \"The rye-spiced, dry bourbon pairs naturally with Honduran Corojo. Shared pepper notes in both.\"}, {\"type\": \"البيرة\", \"name\": \"Artisan porter\", \"notes\": \"The chocolaty depth of an American porter complements the burned coffee نكهات: the Camacho Corojo.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Camacho';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'The CAO story begins with pipes, not cigars. Cano Ozgener, who had emigrated from Turkey to Nashville in the 1960s, founded his business in 1968 as a specialist importer of Turkish briars and Meerschaum pipes — products that his cultural background gave him access to through relationships that American competitors could not replicate. Nashville was an unlikely location for a premium tobacco business, but Ozgener understood that his customer base was not geographic but demographic: the serious pipe collector existed in every American city, and direct mail could reach them without a street-level presence.\r\n\r\nThe transition to cigars in the 1990s was both opportunistic and philosophically motivated. The American cigar boom of that decade was creating demand that the established manufacturers were struggling to meet, and Ozgener recognized in cigar culture the same connoisseurship that he had spent twenty years serving in the pipe market. The customer who had spent years developing their taste in briars was exactly the customer who would appreciate serious cigars, and Ozgener had twenty years of relationship with them.\r\n\r\nCAO\'s early cigar identity was deliberately different from the established houses. Where Arturo Fuente communicated heritage and family continuity, and Davidoff communicated Swiss precision and Cuban ancestry, CAO communicated innovation and cultural reference. The Flathead range, named for and designed around the aesthetic of vintage Harley-Davidson V-twin engines, was the most explicit statement of this identity: a premium cigar that addressed the American enthusiast\'s world directly rather than translating European luxury conventions into tobacco form. The Nicaraguan-Honduran blend inside was serious. The packaging and marketing spoke a language the established Havana-influenced houses would not have recognized.\r\n\r\nGeneral Cigar acquired CAO in 2007, bringing the brand\'s innovative character into a portfolio that needed what Macanudo\'s reliable commercial dominance could not provide. The acquisition has maintained CAO\'s identity as the group\'s risk-taking brand — the release schedule that enthusiasts follow for novelty while they rely on Macanudo for consistency.', `history_es` = 'CAO — las iniciales de Cano Ozgener, fundador turco-americano — nació en Nashville en 1968 como importador de pipas turcas. Evolucionó hacia la fabricación de cigarros en los 90. La Flathead (inspirada en motores Harley V-twin), la Pilon (100% nicaragüense) y la Cameroon son sus gammas más emblemáticas. Adquirida por General Cigar en 2007.', `history_de` = 'CAO — die Initialen von Cano Ozgener, dem türkisch-amerikanischen Gründer — wurde 1968 in Nashville als türkischer Pfeifenimporteur geboren. In den 1990ern entwickelte sie sich zur Zigarrenmanufaktur. Die Flathead (inspiriert von Harley V-Twin-Motoren), die Pilon (100% nicaraguanisch) und die Cameroon sind ihre ikonischsten Serien. 2007 von General Cigar übernommen.', `history_zh` = 'CAO——土裔美国创始人卡诺·奥兹格纳的姓名首字母——1968年在纳什维尔以进口土耳其烟斗起家。20世纪90年代转型为雪茄制造商。Flathead（灵感来自哈雷V型双缸发动机）、Pilon（100%尼加拉瓜）和Cameroon是其最标志性的系列。2007年被通用雪茄收购。', `history_ar` = 'CAO — اختصار اسم كانو أوزغنر المؤسِّس التركي-الأمريكي — وُلد في ناشفيل عام 1968 مستوردًا للغلايين التركية. في التسعينيات تحوَّل إلى صناعة السيجار. الفلات هيد (مستوحى من محركات هارلي V-تويين) والبيلون (100% نيكاراغوا) والكاميرون أكثر تشكيلاته رمزية. استُحوذ عليها General Cigar عام 2007.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"CAO Cameroon\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"Cameroon wrapper over Honduran-Dominican blend. Notes of milk chocolate, hazelnut, soft herbs. Medium, balanced. CAO\'s best-seller in Europe — the Cameroon wrapper brings unique creaminess, slightly sweet on the surface, complex mid-smoke.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"African Cameroon\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Robusto\", \"Corona\", \"Figurado\"]}, {\"name\": \"CAO Flathead\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"Inspired by Harley-Davidson V-twin motorcycles, each format named for an engine part. V660 Carb, V554 Piston, V770 Engine. Ecuadorian wrapper over Nicaraguan-Honduran. Full body, notes of leather, black coffee, chocolate, motor oil (really). A road, freedom, industrial America cigar.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"V660 Carb\", \"V554 Piston\", \"V770 Engine\", \"V507 Spark\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 93, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"CAO Pilon\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"100% Nicaraguan — a political statement in a multi-country blend world. Wrapper, binder, filler: all Nicaragua. Notes of pure coffee, cocoa, black pepper. The range for Nicaraguan terroir purists.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Nicaraguan\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Pyramid\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\": \"CAO Cameroon\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"Cameroon wrapper over Honduran-Dominican blend. Notas de milk chocolate, avellana, soft herbs. Medium, balanced. CAO\'s best-seller in Europe — the Cameroon wrapper brings unique creaminess, slightly sweet on the surface, complex mid-smoke.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"African Cameroon\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Robusto\", \"Corona\", \"Figurado\"]}, {\"name\": \"CAO Flathead\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"Inspired by Harley-Davidson V-twin motorcycles, each format nombrada por an engine part. V660 Carb, V554 Piston, V770 Engine. Ecuadorian wrapper over Nicaraguan-Honduran. Full body, notas de cuero, black café, chocolate, motor oil (really). A road, freedom, industrial America cigar.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"V660 Carb\", \"V554 Piston\", \"V770 Engine\", \"V507 Spark\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 93, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"CAO Pilon\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"100% Nicaraguan — a political statement in a multi-country blend world. Wrapper, binder, filler: all Nicaragua. Notas de pure café, cocoa, pimienta negra. The range for Nicaraguan terroir purists.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Nicaraguan\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Pyramid\"]}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\": \"CAO Cameroon\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"Cameroon wrapper over Honduran-Dominican blend. Noten von milk Schokolade, Haselnuss, soft herbs. Medium, balanced. CAO\'s best-seller in Europe — the Cameroon wrapper brings unique creaminess, slightly sweet on the surface, complex mid-smoke.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"African Cameroon\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Robusto\", \"Corona\", \"Figurado\"]}, {\"name\": \"CAO Flathead\", \"color\": \"#1C0A00\", \"story\": \"Inspired by Harley-Davidson V-twin motorcycles, each format benannt nach an engine part. V660 Carb, V554 Piston, V770 Engine. Ecuadorian wrapper over Nicaraguan-Honduran. Full body, Noten von Leder, black Kaffee, Schokolade, motor oil (really). A road, freedom, industrial America cigar.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian\", \"vitolas\": [\"V660 Carb\", \"V554 Piston\", \"V770 Engine\", \"V507 Spark\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 93, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"CAO Pilon\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"100% Nicaraguan — a political statement in a multi-country blend world. Wrapper, binder, filler: all Nicaragua. Noten von pure Kaffee, cocoa, schwarzer Pfeffer. The range for Nicaraguan terroir purists.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Nicaraguan\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Pyramid\"]}]', `gamme_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"CAO Cameroon\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"Cameroon wrapper over Honduran-Dominican blend. 风味： milk 巧克力, 榛子, soft herbs. Medium, balanced. CAO\'s best-seller in Europe — the Cameroon wrapper brings