: [\"V660 Carb\", \"V554 Piston\", \"V770 Engine\", \"V507 Spark\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 93, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"CAO Pilon\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"100% Nicaraguan — a political statement in a multi-country blend world. Wrapper, binder, filler: all Nicaragua. نكهات:  pure قهوة, cocoa, فلفل أسود. The range for Nicaraguan terroir purists.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Nicaraguan\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Pyramid\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Cano Ozgener\", \"anecdote\": \"The Turkish-American entrepreneur who transformed a Nashville pipe shop into a world manufacturer. He died in 2007, months after the sale to General Cigar. His family says he was satisfied — \'he had created something that would outlast him.\'\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Cano Ozgener\", \"anecdote\": \"The Turkish-American entrepreneur who transformed a Nashville pipe shop into a world manufacturer. He died in 2007, months after the sale to General Cigar. His family says he was satisfied — \'he had created something that would outlast him.\'\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Cano Ozgener\", \"anecdote\": \"The Turkish-American entrepreneur who transformed a Nashville pipe shop into a world manufacturer. He died in 2007, months after the sale to General Cigar. His family says he was satisfied — \'he had created something that would outlast him.\'\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Cano Ozgener\", \"anecdote\": \"The Turkish-American entrepreneur who transformed a Nashville pipe shop into a world manufacturer. He died in 2007, months after the sale to General Cigar. His family says he was satisfied — \'he had created something that would outlast him.\'\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Cano Ozgener\", \"anecdote\": \"The Turkish-American entrepreneur who transformed a Nashville pipe shop into a world manufacturer. He died in 2007, months after the sale to General Cigar. His family says he was satisfied — \'he had created something that would outlast him.\'\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Coffee\", \"name\": \"Turkish coffee\", \"notes\": \"A tribute to the founder\'s origins — the thick, intense Turkish coffee perfectly accompanies the 100% Nicaraguan Pilon.\"}, {\"type\": \"Beer\", \"name\": \"Harley-Davidson Official Lager\", \"notes\": \"The perfect marketing pairing for the Flathead — both brands share the aesthetic of the American open road.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\": \"Café\", \"name\": \"Turkish coffee\", \"notes\": \"A tribute to the founder\'s origins — the thick, intense Turkish coffee acompaña perfectamente the 100% Nicaraguan Pilon.\"}, {\"type\": \"Cerveza\", \"name\": \"Harley-Davidson Official Lager\", \"notes\": \"The perfect marketing pairing for the Flathead — both brands share the aesthetic of the American open road.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\": \"Kaffee\", \"name\": \"Turkish coffee\", \"notes\": \"A tribute to the founder\'s origins — the thick, intense Turkish coffee perfectly accompanies the 100% Nicaraguan Pilon.\"}, {\"type\": \"Bier\", \"name\": \"Harley-Davidson Official Lager\", \"notes\": \"The perfect marketing pairing for the Flathead — both brands share the aesthetic of the American open road.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\": \"咖啡\", \"name\": \"Turkish coffee\", \"notes\": \"A tribute to the founder\'s origins — the thick, intense Turkish coffee 完美搭配 the 100% Nicaraguan Pilon.\"}, {\"type\": \"啤酒\", \"name\": \"Harley-Davidson Official Lager\", \"notes\": \"The perfect marketing pairing for the Flathead — both brands share the aesthetic of the American open road.\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\": \"القهوة\", \"name\": \"Turkish coffee\", \"notes\": \"A tribute to the founder\'s origins — the thick, intense Turkish coffee perfectly accompanies the 100% Nicaraguan Pilon.\"}, {\"type\": \"البيرة\", \"name\": \"Harley-Davidson Official Lager\", \"notes\": \"The perfect marketing pairing for the Flathead — both brands share the aesthetic of the American open road.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'CAO';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'CAO America is a declaration of independence — not political, but agricultural. Launched in 2004, it arrived at a moment when the premium cigar world had become entirely preoccupied with Nicaraguan power and Honduran earthiness. The conversation was always about Central American terroir. CAO\'s response was to look north, to the tobacco fields that had supplied American smokers for three centuries before the Cuban revolution and the Nicaraguan boom reshaped the market.\r\n\r\nThe concept is straightforward and almost defiantly specific: 100% American tobacco in every component. The wrappers come from Connecticut\'s river valley, where the famously sandy loam soil produces the most celebrated shade-grown leaf in the Americas — the standard against which every other Connecticut-style wrapper is measured. The binders draw from Pennsylvania\'s Lancaster County, where broadleaf tobacco has been grown since the 17th century. The fillers blend leaf from Virginia, where tobacco cultivation predates the United States itself, and from Connecticut once more.\r\n\r\nWhat this creates, technically, is a cigar entirely outside the Central American flavor profile that dominates the premium sector. CAO America profiles are rounder, gentler, and more herbaceous than Nicaraguan cigars. They share the creamy texture that good Connecticut shade naturally produces, with underlying notes of dried grass, warm cedar, and the mild nuttiness of well-cured Pennsylvania leaf. The medium-body strength allows the tobacco\'s character to express itself without the aggressive pepper and earth notes that mark the Nicaraguan style.\r\n\r\nThe range initially faced skepticism from retailers accustomed to selling intensity. American tobacco had been associated, somewhat unfairly, with the machine-made mass market rather than the artisanal premium sector. CAO America challenged that prejudice directly, positioning itself as the product of a deliberate terroir choice rather than a concession to commercial calculation. The subsequent success of the range — particularly in markets where smokers preferred elegance to power — validated the bet.', `history_es` = 'CAO America celebra el terroir tabacalero americano. Lanzada en 2004, explora las regiones tradicionales: Connecticut, Pensilvania, Virginia. Una apuesta nacionalista que usa tabaco 100% americano en sus principales gamas.', `history_de` = 'CAO America feiert das amerikanische Tabak-Terroir. 2004 lanciert, erkundet sie die traditionellen Regionen: Connecticut, Pennsylvania, Virginia. Eine nationalistische Wette mit 100% amerikanischem Tabak in ihren Hauptserien.', `history_zh` = 'CAO America赞美美国烟草风土。2004年推出，探索传统产区：康涅狄格、宾夕法尼亚、弗吉尼亚。主要系列使用100%美国烟草，一场民族主义的赌注。', `history_ar` = 'تُحتفي CAO America بتراب التبغ الأمريكي. أُطلقت عام 2004، تستكشف المناطق التقليدية: كونيكتيكت وبنسلفانيا وفيرجينيا. رهان قومي يستخدم تبغًا أمريكيًا 100% في تشكيلاتها الرئيسية.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\":\"CAO America Potomac\",\"color\":\"#B22222\",\"story\":\"Toro format. Pennsylvania-Virginia blend, Connecticut wrapper. Notes of dried hay, red fruit, light acidity. Medium. The most accessible range of the America series — an introduction to American terroir.\",\"force\":\"Medium\",\"wrapper\":\"Connecticut Shade\",\"vitolas\":[\"Potomac\",\"Gettysburg\",\"Monument\"]},{\"name\":\"CAO America Landmark\",\"color\":\"#1C3A6E\",\"story\":\"Full-bodied American — Connecticut Broadleaf wrapper over Virginia ligero. Notes of American cedar, walnut, autumn spices. The powerful face of the series. Churchill format recommended for the full aromatic evolution.\",\"force\":\"Full\",\"wrapper\":\"Connecticut Broadleaf\",\"vitolas\":[\"Landmark\",\"Monument\",\"Toro\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\":\"CAO America Potomac\",\"color\":\"#B22222\",\"story\":\"Formato Toro. Ligada de Pensilvania y Virginia con capa Connecticut. Notas de heno seco, frutos rojos y ligera acidez. Medio. La gama más asequible de la serie America: una introducción al terruño estadounidense.\",\"force\":\"Medium\",\"wrapper\":\"Connecticut Shade\",\"vitolas\":[\"Potomac\",\"Gettysburg\",\"Monument\"]},{\"name\":\"CAO America Landmark\",\"color\":\"#1C3A6E\",\"story\":\"Americano de cuerpo pleno: capa Connecticut Broadleaf sobre ligero de Virginia. Notas de cedro americano, nuez y especias otoñales. La cara potente de la serie. Se recomienda el formato Churchill para la evolución aromática completa.\",\"force\":\"Full\",\"wrapper\":\"Connecticut Broadleaf\",\"vitolas\":[\"Landmark\",\"Monument\",\"Toro\"]}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\":\"CAO America Potomac\",\"color\":\"#B22222\",\"story\":\"Format Toro. Mischung aus Pennsylvania und Virginia mit Connecticut-Deckblatt. Noten von getrocknetem Heu, roten Früchten, leichter Säure. Medium. Die zugänglichste Linie der America-Serie — eine Einführung in das amerikanische Terroir.\",\"force\":\"Medium\",\"wrapper\":\"Connecticut Shade\",\"vitolas\":[\"Potomac\",\"Gettysburg\",\"Monument\"]},{\"name\":\"CAO America Landmark\",\"color\":\"#1C3A6E\",\"story\":\"Kräftiger Amerikaner — Connecticut-Broadleaf-Deckblatt über Virginia-Ligero. Noten von amerikanischer Zeder, Walnuss und herbstlichen Gewürzen. Das kraftvolle Gesicht der Serie. Für die vollständige aromatische Entwicklung empfiehlt sich das Churchill-Format.\",\"force\":\"Full\",\"wrapper\":\"Connecticut Broadleaf\",\"vitolas\":[\"Landmark\",\"Monument\",\"Toro\"]}]', `gamme_zh` = '[{\"name\":\"CAO America Potomac\",\"color\":\"#B22222\",\"story\":\"Toro 规格。宾夕法尼亚与弗吉尼亚配方，Connecticut 茄衣。干草、红色浆果的气息，带轻微酸度。中度。America 系列中最易入手的一条线——美国风土的入门。\",\"force\":\"Medium\",\"wrapper\":\"Connecticut Shade\",\"vitolas\":[\"Potomac\",\"Gettysburg\",\"Monument\"]},{\"name\":\"CAO America Landmark\",\"color\":\"#1C3A6E\",\"story\":\"浓郁的美国风格——Connecticut Broadleaf 茄衣，配弗吉尼亚 ligero。美洲雪松、核桃与秋日香料的气息。系列中强劲的一面。想领略完整的香气演变，推荐 Churchill 规格。\",\"force\":\"Full\",\"wrapper\":\"Connecticut Broadleaf\",\"vitolas\":[\"Landmark\",\"Monument\",\"Toro\"]}]', `gamme_ar` = '[{\"name\":\"CAO America Potomac\",\"color\":\"#B22222\",\"story\":\"طراز Toro. خلطة من بنسلفانيا وفرجينيا بغلاف Connecticut. لمسات من القشّ المجفَّف والفواكه الحمراء وحموضة خفيفة. متوسط. وهي أيسر تشكيلات سلسلة America تناولاً — ومدخل إلى الأرض الأمريكية.\",\"force\":\"Medium\",\"wrapper\":\"Connecticut Shade\",\"vitolas\":[\"Potomac\",\"Gettysburg\",\"Monument\"]},{\"name\":\"CAO America Landmark\",\"color\":\"#1C3A6E\",\"story\":\"أمريكي كامل الجسم — غلاف Connecticut Broadleaf على Virginia ligero. لمسات من الأرز الأمريكي والجوز وتوابل الخريف. إنه الوجه القوي للسلسلة. ويُنصح بطراز Churchill لمتابعة التطوّر العطري كاملاً.\",\"force\":\"Full\",\"wrapper\":\"Connecticut Broadleaf\",\"vitolas\":[\"Landmark\",\"Monument\",\"Toro\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[]', `celebrities_es` = '[]', `celebrities_de` = '[]', `celebrities_zh` = '[]', `celebrities_ar` = '[]', `pairings_en` = '[]', `pairings_es` = '[]', `pairings_de` = '[]', `pairings_zh` = '[]', `pairings_ar` = '[]' WHERE `name` = 'CAO America';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'The Mexican San Andrés valley sits in the state of Veracruz, between the Gulf of Mexico coast and the Orizaba volcanic range, at elevations between 800 and 1,200 meters. The combination of volcanic soil, consistent humidity from Gulf air masses, and altitude-modulated temperatures creates conditions that produce tobacco unlike any other in the Americas. San Andrés leaf is dark — naturally, without the extended fermentation that produces Connecticut or Brazilian Maduro — and carries a specific bitterness that blenders prize for its ability to anchor a blend against the sweetness of lighter fillers.\r\n\r\nThe San Andrés Maduro wrapper used in CAO Black is this terroir taken to its logical extreme. The already-dark natural San Andrés leaf is subjected to extended fermentation that pushes its color toward near-black and transforms its natural bitterness into a complex spice character. The result is the darkest commercially available Honduran-blend wrapper in the major American catalog — not in the artificial sense of added color, but in the genuine agricultural sense of leaf that has fermented at maximum intensity without structural failure.\r\n\r\nOver the Nicaraguan-Honduran filler blend that CAO uses throughout its premium catalog, this wrapper creates a profile of exceptional distinctiveness. The first third delivers pure cocoa — not sweetened, not diluted, but the aggressive bitterness of unsweetened baking chocolate. The middle third introduces licorice and Cayenne pepper in a combination that recalls the flavor profile of Mexican mole sauce, which is not coincidental: the same San Andrés pepper-growing tradition that produces the region\'s famous chiles exists alongside its tobacco cultivation. The final third resolves toward a long, warming finish of dark spice and espresso.\r\n\r\nCAO Black positions itself as the most challenging proposition in the CAO catalog — a cigar for smokers who have moved past the preference for sweetness and cream that dominates the Connecticut and Cameroon ranges and are deliberately seeking intensity and complexity. It has found a dedicated audience among enthusiasts who find full-body Nicaraguan cigars too linear and are looking for the specific aromatic dimension that only dark Mexican wrapper can provide.', `history_es` = 'La gama Black de CAO utiliza el envolvente mexicano San Andrés Maduro — la hoja más oscura de Veracruz. Sobre un blend nicaragüense-hondureño, este envolvente mexicano crea un perfil chocolateado e intenso. Notas de cacao puro, regaliz, pimienta de Cayena.', `history_de` = 'Die Black-Linie von CAO verwendet den mexikanischen San-Andrés-Maduro-Wrapper — das dunkelste Blatt aus Veracruz. Über einem nicaraguanisch-honduranischen Blend schafft dieser mexikanische Wrapper ein schokoladiges, intensives Profil. Noten von reinem Kakao, Lakritze, Cayennepfeffer.', `history_zh` = 'CAO的黑色系列使用墨西哥圣安德烈斯马杜罗茄衣——韦拉克鲁斯最深色的叶片。覆盖尼加拉瓜-洪都拉斯混合烟叶，这款墨西哥茄衣创造出巧克力感、强烈的轮廓。纯可可、甘草、卡宴辣椒风味。', `history_ar` = 'تشكيلة بلاك من CAO تستخدم الغلافة المكسيكية سان أندريس مادورو — أكثر أوراق فيراكروز قتامةً. فوق خلطة نيكاراغوية-هندوراسية، تُنتج هذه الغلافة ملفًا شوكولاتيًا مكثفًا. نكهات الكاكاو الخالص وعرق السوس والفلفل الأحمر.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\":\"CAO Black\",\"color\":\"#1C0A00\",\"story\":\"Mexican San Andrés Maduro wrapper over Nicaraguan-Honduran filler. Notes of dark cocoa, liquorice, cayenne pepper. Full body. CAO\'s dark side — powerful, direct, uncompromising. Toro format recommended for maximum complexity.\",\"force\":\"Full\",\"wrapper\":\"Mexican San Andrés Maduro\",\"vitolas\":[\"Robusto\",\"Toro\",\"Churchill\",\"Torpedo\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\":\"CAO Black\",\"color\":\"#1C0A00\",\"story\":\"Capa Mexican San Andrés Maduro sobre tripa nicaragüense y hondureña. Notas de cacao negro, regaliz y pimienta de Cayena. Cuerpo pleno. El lado oscuro de CAO: potente, directo, sin concesiones. Se recomienda el formato Toro para la máxima complejidad.\",\"force\":\"Full\",\"wrapper\":\"Mexican San Andrés Maduro\",\"vitolas\":[\"Robusto\",\"Toro\",\"Churchill\",\"Torpedo\"]}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\":\"CAO Black\",\"color\":\"#1C0A00\",\"story\":\"Mexikanisches San-Andrés-Maduro-Deckblatt über nicaraguanisch-honduranischer Einlage. Noten von dunklem Kakao, Lakritz und Cayennepfeffer. Voller Körper. Die dunkle Seite von CAO — kraftvoll, direkt, kompromisslos. Für höchste Komplexität empfiehlt sich das Toro-Format.\",\"force\":\"Full\",\"wrapper\":\"Mexican San Andrés Maduro\",\"vitolas\":[\"Robusto\",\"Toro\",\"Churchill\",\"Torpedo\"]}]', `gamme_zh` = '[{\"name\":\"CAO Black\",\"color\":\"#1C0A00\",\"story\":\"墨西哥 San Andrés Maduro 茄衣，配尼加拉瓜与洪都拉斯填充。黑可可、甘草与卡宴辣椒的气息。full body。这是 CAO 的暗面——强劲、直接、毫不妥协。追求最大层次感，推荐 Toro 规格。\",\"force\":\"Full\",\"wrapper\":\"Mexican San Andrés Maduro\",\"vitolas\":[\"Robusto\",\"Toro\",\"Churchill\",\"Torpedo\"]}]', `gamme_ar` = '[{\"name\":\"CAO Black\",\"color\":\"#1C0A00\",\"story\":\"غلاف San Andrés Maduro المكسيكي على حشوة نيكاراغوية هندوراسية. لمسات من الكاكاو الداكن وعرق السوس وفلفل الكايين. جسم كامل. إنه الوجه المعتم لـ CAO — قوي، مباشر، بلا مساومة. ويُنصح بطراز Toro لأقصى تعقيد.\",\"force\":\"Full\",\"wrapper\":\"Mexican San Andrés Maduro\",\"vitolas\":[\"Robusto\",\"Toro\",\"Churchill\",\"Torpedo\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[]', `celebrities_es` = '[]', `celebrities_de` = '[]', `celebrities_zh` = '[]', `celebrities_ar` = '[]', `pairings_en` = '[]', `pairings_es` = '[]', `pairings_de` = '[]', `pairings_zh` = '[]', `pairings_ar` = '[]' WHERE `name` = 'CAO Black';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'The story of Cameroonian tobacco in premium cigars is largely a story of discovery delayed by geography. The Centre province of Cameroon — a region of equatorial soils, consistent humidity, and temperatures that barely vary month to month — produces a wrapper leaf unlike anything grown in the Americas. It is darker in color than Connecticut shade, more complex in structure, and carries a natural oil content that makes it visually distinctive and aromatically potent from the moment the cigar is cut.\r\n\r\nCAO was among the first American manufacturers to build an entire range around this terroir. The CAO Cameroon line uses the AVO XO wrapper — a specific selection from the Centre province that represents the top tier of Cameroonian leaf reaching the American market. The wrapper\'s complexity is immediately evident: a pronounced cocoa character that sits between milk chocolate and dark, combined with a natural sweetness that counters rather than amplifies the blend\'s spice. The effect is a profile of unusual sophistication for a mid-priced range.\r\n\r\nThe blend beneath the Cameroonian wrapper uses Dominican and Brazilian fillers chosen to complement rather than compete with the wrapper\'s character. The result is a cigar that leads with chocolate and soft pepper on the first third, develops toward coffee and dried cherry in the middle, and finishes with a long, slightly sweet cedar note that demonstrates how well-selected wrapper tobacco can transform an otherwise conventional Nicaraguan-Dominican blend into something memorable.\r\n\r\nCameroonian tobacco reached serious attention in the premium market partly through CAO\'s advocacy and partly through its use in Davidoff\'s prized Millennium series. Once major manufacturers began sourcing it aggressively, the available supply tightened considerably. CAO Cameroon\'s position as an early adopter gives it a sourcing relationship with Central African growers that newer entrants to the category have struggled to match.', `history_es` = 'Gama emblemática de CAO que utiliza el envolvente camerunés AVO XO. El tabaco de Camerún desarrolla una cremosidad y complejidad chocolateada únicas. CAO fue una de las primeras casas americanas en destacar este terroir africano.', `history_de` = 'CAOs emblematische Serie mit dem kamerunischen AVO XO Wrapper. Der kamerunische Tabak entwickelt eine einzigartige Cremigkeit und schokoladige Komplexität. CAO war eines der ersten amerikanischen Häuser, das dieses afrikanische Terroir in den Vordergrund stellte.', `history_zh` = 'CAO的标志性系列，使用喀麦隆AVO XO茄衣。喀麦隆烟草形成了独特的奶油感和巧克力复杂性。CAO是最早突显这一非洲风土的美国品牌之一。', `history_ar` = 'تشكيلة CAO الرمزية التي تستخدم الغلافة الكاميرونية AVO XO. يُنمِّي التبغ الكاميروني نعومةً وتعقيدًا شوكولاتيًا فريدَين. كانت CAO من أوائل الدور الأمريكية التي سلَّطت الضوء على هذا التربة الأفريقية.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\":\"CAO Cameroon\",\"color\":\"#8B6914\",\"story\":\"Cameroonian wrapper over a Honduran-Dominican blend. Notes of milk chocolate, hazelnut, mild herbs. Balanced medium. CAO\'s best-selling range in Europe — the African wrapper brings a silkiness that American or Caribbean wrappers cannot reproduce.\",\"force\":\"Medium\",\"wrapper\":\"African Cameroon AVO XO\",\"vitolas\":[\"Toro\",\"Churchill\",\"Robusto\",\"Figurado\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\":\"CAO Cameroon\",\"color\":\"#8B6914\",\"story\":\"Capa camerunesa sobre ligada hondureño-dominicana. Notas de chocolate con leche, avellana y hierbas suaves. Medio equilibrado. La gama más vendida de CAO en Europa: la capa africana aporta una untuosidad que las capas americanas o caribeñas no logran reproducir.\",\"force\":\"Medium\",\"wrapper\":\"African Cameroon AVO XO\",\"vitolas\":[\"Toro\",\"Churchill\",\"Robusto\",\"Figurado\"]}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\":\"CAO Cameroon\",\"color\":\"#8B6914\",\"story\":\"Kamerun-Deckblatt über einer honduranisch-dominikanischen Mischung. Noten von Milchschokolade, Haselnuss und milden Kräutern. Ausgewogenes Medium. Die meistverkaufte CAO-Linie Europas — das afrikanische Deckblatt bringt eine Geschmeidigkeit, die amerikanische oder karibische Deckblätter nicht nachbilden können.\",\"force\":\"Medium\",\"wrapper\":\"African Cameroon AVO XO\",\"vitolas\":[\"Toro\",\"Churchill\",\"Robusto\",\"Figurado\"]}]', `gamme_zh` = '[{\"name\":\"CAO Cameroon\",\"color\":\"#8B6914\",\"story\":\"喀麦隆茄衣，配洪都拉斯与多米尼加填充。牛奶巧克力、榛果与柔和草本的气息。均衡的中度。这是 CAO 在欧洲销量最高的一条线——非洲茄衣带来的那份润滑，美洲或加勒比茄衣都复制不来。\",\"force\":\"Medium\",\"wrapper\":\"African Cameroon AVO XO\",\"vitolas\":[\"Toro\",\"Churchill\",\"Robusto\",\"Figurado\"]}]', `gamme_ar` = '[{\"name\":\"CAO Cameroon\",\"color\":\"#8B6914\",\"story\":\"غلاف كاميروني على خلطة هندوراسية دومينيكية. لمسات من شوكولاتة الحليب والبندق والأعشاب اللطيفة. متوسط متوازن. وهي أكثر تشكيلات CAO مبيعاً في أوروبا — إذ يمنح الغلاف الأفريقي نعومة لا تستطيع أغلفة الأمريكتين أو الكاريبي محاكاتها.\",\"force\":\"Medium\",\"wrapper\":\"African Cameroon AVO XO\",\"vitolas\":[\"Toro\",\"Churchill\",\"Robusto\",\"Figurado\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[]', `celebrities_es` = '[]', `celebrities_de` = '[]', `celebrities_zh` = '[]', `celebrities_ar` = '[]', `pairings_en` = '[]', `pairings_es` = '[]', `pairings_de` = '[]', `pairings_zh` = '[]', `pairings_ar` = '[]' WHERE `name` = 'CAO Cameroon';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'Carlos Toraño established one of Havana\'s most important tobacco export houses in 1916, building over four decades a business that connected Cuban leaf to European manufacturers who depended on Vuelta Abajo tobacco for their premium lines. The Toraños understood tobacco as a trade commodity before they understood it as a craft product, and this commercial perspective — the ability to read markets, build relationships, and move product across distances — would prove more durable than any specific growing knowledge when the revolution ended their Cuban operation in 1959.\r\n\r\nThe diaspora years followed a path shared by many Cuban tobacco families: Miami first, where the exile community maintained the professional networks that made immediate re-employment possible, then a longer search for the growing conditions and operational scale that would allow genuine production rather than mere distribution. Panama entered the calculation through a combination of political stability, available land, and altitude that the Toraños identified as potentially suitable for the quality they intended to maintain.\r\n\r\nThe Chiriquí Province in western Panama, near the Costa Rican border, offers growing conditions that serious tobacologists find more interesting than Panama\'s general agricultural reputation would suggest. The highland areas above Boquete, at elevations between 1,200 and 1,800 meters, receive consistent rainfall from both Pacific and Caribbean air masses, producing a combination of moisture and temperature variation that slows tobacco leaf development in ways that concentrate aromatic compounds. The resulting leaf is not powerful — it lacks the pepper and earth of Nicaraguan tobacco and the chocolate intensity of Honduran — but it possesses a restrained elegance that blenders with specific ambitions have found useful.\r\n\r\nThe Exodus 1959 range, named for the year the family left Cuba, represents the Toraños\' most personal statement: cigars that acknowledge displacement explicitly while demonstrating that the knowledge displaced from Cuba has found a new expression in soil the family chose for its own qualities rather than as a consolation for what was lost. The blend uses Chiriquí tobaccos in combination with Dominican and Nicaraguan leaf, the multiple origins reflecting the family\'s multi-country trajectory as much as any technical blending logic.', `history_es` = 'Carlos Toraño fue uno de los grandes tabacaleros de Cuba. Tras la revolución, la familia se instaló en Miami y luego en Panamá, donde cultivan y producen desde hace más de 60 años. Las plantaciones en la Provincia de Chiriquí, a gran altitud, producen un tabaco de elegancia discreta. La gama Exodus 1959 es su memoria fumable.', `history_de` = 'Carlos Toraño war einer der großen kubanischen Tabakexperten. Nach der Revolution ließ sich die Familie zunächst in Miami, dann in Panama nieder, wo sie seit über 60 Jahren anbaut und produziert. Die Plantagen in der Provinz Chiriquí in großer Höhe produzieren Tabak von diskreter Eleganz. Die Exodus 1959-Linie ist ihr rauchbares Gedächtnis.', `history_zh` = '卡洛斯·托拉尼奥是古巴最伟大的烟草专家之一。革命后，家族先定居迈阿密，后移居巴拿马，在那里种植和生产已超过60年。奇里基省高海拔种植园生产着一种具有低调优雅气质的烟草。Exodus 1959系列是他们可吸食的记忆。', `history_ar` = 'كان كارلوس تورانيو من كبار خبراء التبغ في كوبا. بعد الثورة، استقرت العائلة في ميامي ثم بنما، حيث يزرعون وينتجون منذ أكثر من 60 عامًا. مزارع إقليم تشيريكي على الارتفاعات تنتج تبغًا بأناقة خافتة. تشكيلة إكسودوس 1959 هي ذاكرتهم الدخانية.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Carlos Toraño Exodus 1959\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"Named for the 1959 exile. Connecticut Shade wrapper over Dominican-Nicaraguan blend. Notes of cream, nuts, light wood. Medium, soft. A tribute to Cuba without bitter nostalgia — an elegant cigar looking forward.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Connecticut Shade\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Corona\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 91, \"year\": 2019}]}, {\"name\": \"Carlos Toraño Casa Toraño\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Full body Honduran-Nicaraguan, oscuro wrapper. Notes of coffee, pepper, dark undergrowth. The powerful range for enthusiasts seeking Central American intensity. Toro format recommended.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Torpedo\"]}, {\"name\": \"Exodus Silver\", \"color\": \"#C0C0C0\", \"story\": \"Connecticut Shade wrapper, Dominican blend. Light-Medium. The house\'s gentle face — accessible, consistent. The entry into the Toraño universe for beginners.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Connecticut Shade\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Carlos Toraño Exodus 1959\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"Nombrada por the 1959 exile. Connecticut Shade wrapper over Dominican-Nicaraguan blend. Notas de cream, nuts, light wood. Medium, soft. A tribute to Cuba without bitter nostalgia — an elegant cigar looking forward.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Connecticut Shade\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Corona\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 91, \"year\": 2019}]}, {\"name\": \"Carlos Toraño Casa Toraño\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Full body Honduran-Nicaraguan, oscuro wrapper. Notas de café, pimienta, dark undergrowth. The powerful range for aficionados seeking Central American intensity. Toro format recommended.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Torpedo\"]}, {\"name\": \"Exodus Silver\", \"color\": \"#C0C0C0\", \"story\": \"Connecticut Shade wrapper, Dominican blend. Light-Medium. La gentle face — accessible, consistent. The entry into the Toraño universe for beginners.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Connecticut Shade\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Carlos Toraño Exodus 1959\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"Benannt nach the 1959 exile. Connecticut Shade wrapper over Dominican-Nicaraguan blend. Noten von cream, nuts, light wood. Medium, soft. A tribute to Cuba without bitter nostalgia — an elegant cigar looking forward.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Connecticut Shade\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Corona\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 91, \"year\": 2019}]}, {\"name\": \"Carlos Toraño Casa Toraño\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Full body Honduran-Nicaraguan, oscuro wrapper. Noten von Kaffee, Pfeffer, dark undergrowth. The powerful range for enthusiasts seeking Central American intensity. Toro format recommended.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Torpedo\"]}, {\"name\": \"Exodus Silver\", \"color\": \"#C0C0C0\", \"story\": \"Connecticut Shade wrapper, Dominican blend. Light-Medium. The house\'s gentle face — accessible, consistent. The entry into the Toraño universe for beginners.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Connecticut Shade\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Carlos Toraño Exodus 1959\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"以…命名 the 1959 exile. Connecticut Shade wrapper over Dominican-Nicaraguan blend. 风味： cream, nuts, light wood. Medium, soft. A tribute to Cuba without bitter nostalgia — an elegant cigar looking forward.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Connecticut Shade\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Corona\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 91, \"year\": 2019}]}, {\"name\": \"Carlos Toraño Casa Toraño\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Full body Honduran-Nicaraguan, oscuro wrapper. 风味： 咖啡, 胡椒, dark undergrowth. The powerful range for 爱好者 seeking Central American intensity. Toro format recommended.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Torpedo\"]}, {\"name\": \"Exodus Silver\", \"color\": \"#C0C0C0\", \"story\": \"Connecticut Shade wrapper, Dominican blend. Light-Medium. The house\'s gentle face — accessible, consistent. The entry into the Toraño universe for beginners.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Connecticut Shade\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `gamme_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Carlos Toraño Exodus 1959\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"سُمِّيت تيمنًا بـ the 1959 exile. Connecticut Shade wrapper over Dominican-Nicaraguan blend. نكهات:  cream, nuts, light wood. Medium, soft. A tribute to Cuba without bitter nostalgia — an elegant cigar looking forward.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Connecticut Shade\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\", \"Torpedo\", \"Corona\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 91, \"year\": 2019}]}, {\"name\": \"Carlos Toraño Casa Toraño\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Full body Honduran-Nicaraguan, oscuro wrapper. نكهات:  قهوة, فلفل, dark undergrowth. The powerful range for المتحمسون seeking Central American intensity. Toro format recommended.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Honduran Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Torpedo\"]}, {\"name\": \"Exodus Silver\", \"color\": \"#C0C0C0\", \"story\": \"Connecticut Shade wrapper, Dominican blend. Light-Medium. The house\'s gentle face — accessible, consistent. The entry into the Toraño universe for beginners.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Connecticut Shade\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Churchill\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Toraño Family\", \"anecdote\": \"Four generations who survived the Cuban revolution, exile, and decades of economic uncertainty without ever abandoning tobacco. The Exodus 1959 range is their smokable memory — each box bears the date that changed their lives forever.\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Toraño Family\", \"anecdote\": \"Four generations who survived the Cuban revolution, exile, and decades of economic uncertainty without ever abandoning tobacco. The Exodus 1959 range is their smokable memory — each box bears the date that changed their lives forever.\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Toraño Family\", \"anecdote\": \"Four generations who survived the Cuban revolution, exile, and decades of economic uncertainty without ever abandoning tobacco. The Exodus 1959 range is their smokable memory — each box bears the date that changed their lives forever.\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Toraño Family\", \"anecdote\": \"Four generations who survived the Cuban revolution, exile, and decades of economic uncertainty without ever abandoning tobacco. The Exodus 1959 range is their smokable memory — each box bears the date that changed their lives forever.\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Toraño Family\", \"anecdote\": \"Four generations who survived the Cuban revolution, exile, and decades of economic uncertainty without ever abandoning tobacco. The Exodus 1959 range is their smokable memory — each box bears the date that changed their lives forever.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Rum\", \"name\": \"Ron Abuelo 12 years\", \"notes\": \"Panama\'s prestige rum naturally accompanies Toraño\'s Panamanian productions. Two excellences from the same country.\"}, {\"type\": \"Coffee\", \"name\": \"Chiriquí coffee\", \"notes\": \"Coffee from the same province as the Toraño plantations — a Panamanian terroir pairing.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\": \"Ron\", \"name\": \"Ron Abuelo 12 years\", \"notes\": \"Panama\'s prestige rum acompaña naturalmente Toraño\'s Panamanian productions. Two excellences from the same country.\"}, {\"type\": \"Café\", \"name\": \"Chiriquí coffee\", \"notes\": \"Coffee from the same province as the Toraño plantations — a Panamanian terroir pairing.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\": \"Rum\", \"name\": \"Ron Abuelo 12 years\", \"notes\": \"Panama\'s prestige rum naturally accompanies Toraño\'s Panamanian productions. Two excellences from the same country.\"}, {\"type\": \"Kaffee\", \"name\": \"Chiriquí coffee\", \"notes\": \"Coffee from the same province as the Toraño plantations — a Panamanian terroir pairing.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\": \"朗姆酒\", \"name\": \"Ron Abuelo 12 years\", \"notes\": \"Panama\'s prestige rum naturally accompanies Toraño\'s Panamanian productions. Two excellences from the same country.\"}, {\"type\": \"咖啡\", \"name\": \"Chiriquí coffee\", \"notes\": \"Coffee from the same province as the Toraño plantations — a Panamanian terroir pairing.\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\": \"الروم\", \"name\": \"Ron Abuelo 12 years\", \"notes\": \"Panama\'s prestige rum naturally accompanies Toraño\'s Panamanian productions. Two excellences from the same country.\"}, {\"type\": \"القهوة\", \"name\": \"Chiriquí coffee\", \"notes\": \"Coffee from the same province as the Toraño plantations — a Panamanian terroir pairing.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Carlos Toraño Panama';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'Cohiba was born in absolute secrecy in 1966. Eduardo Rivera, a torcedor whose exceptional private cigars had caught the eye of a presidential bodyguard, was summoned to Havana and quietly installed at El Laguito — a former aristocratic mansion in the Miramar district. For sixteen years, Cohiba was never sold. It existed as a diplomatic instrument: boxes without price tags, offered by Fidel Castro to heads of state who understood immediately they held something extraordinary. Willy Brandt received them in Bonn. François Mitterrand in Paris. Muammar Gaddafi in Tripoli. Nelson Mandela in Johannesburg. All received boxes of this nameless cigar.\r\n\r\nIn 1982, facing mounting international curiosity and a growing black market, Cuba opened Cohiba to commercial distribution — but only outside the island, and only through Cubatabaco\'s most exclusive channels. The name comes from the Taíno language, spoken by Cuba\'s original inhabitants before Columbus: it simply means tobacco. The irony is perfect — the world\'s most prestigious cigar bears the most ancient and universal name for what it is.\r\n\r\nWhat makes Cohiba technically distinct is the third fermentation. After the standard two fermentations undergone by all Cuban tobacco, Cohiba\'s leaves undergo a third extended fermentation in cedar barrels. This process, closely guarded and unique in the industry, extracts a final layer of harshness and develops the complex, almost creamy equilibrium that defines the brand\'s profile. The leaves come exclusively from Vuelta Abajo, Cuba\'s most prestigious growing region, and are selected personally by the factory\'s master blenders.\r\n\r\nEl Laguito is Cohiba\'s world. Its workforce is predominantly female — the torcedoras who roll Cohiba are Cuba\'s highest-paid cigar artisans. The factory does not receive visitors. Its rhythms are its own. Each cigar leaving El Laguito passes through more quality control checkpoints than any other Cuban brand. Rejected cigars — roughly one in five — are destroyed, never redistributed.\r\n\r\nThe Cohiba band, with its distinctive black and yellow design, has become a universal symbol of status extending far beyond the tobacco world. It appears in film, literature, and political photography as shorthand for power. It is also the world\'s most counterfeited cigar band — a distinction that measures the brand\'s reach better than any sales figure.\r\n\r\nToday, Cohiba stands as the undisputed apex of Cuban tobacco. The Behike BHK line, launched in 2010 for the brand\'s 44th anniversary, pushed the concept further still: using the ultra-rare medio tiempo leaf — found only at the very crown of the tobacco plant, in quantities too small to harvest at scale — it produced what many experts consider the most complex cigar ever commercially released. Fewer than three thousand boxes exist per year. The waiting lists are longer than the cigar itself.', `history_es` = 'Cohiba nació en el mayor secreto para servir a Fidel Castro. Eduardo Rivera, torcedor cuyos cigarros personales habían llamado la atención de un guardaespaldas de Castro, fue convocado a La Habana. Durante dieciséis años, Cohiba nunca se comercializó — solo se ofrecía como regalo diplomático a jefes de Estado. Brandt, Mitterrand y Gaddafi recibieron cajas de este cigarro sin nombre.\r\n\r\nEn 1982, ante la creciente demanda diplomática, Cuba abrió Cohiba al comercio internacional. El nombre proviene del vocablo taíno — lengua de los primeros habitantes de Cuba — que significa tabaco. Cohiba es hoy la marca de cigarros más reconocida, más falsificada y más codiciada del mundo.\r\n\r\nLa fábrica El Laguito, ubicada en una antigua mansión habanera, es el santuario de la marca. Sus torcedoras — en su mayoría mujeres — son las artesanas del cigarro mejor pagadas de Cuba. Fumar un Cohiba es inhalar seis décadas de historia revolucionaria.', `history_de` = 'Cohiba wurde im strengsten Geheimnis geboren, um Fidel Castro zu dienen. Eduardo Rivera, ein Torcedor, dessen außergewöhnliche persönliche Zigarren einem Leibwächter Castros aufgefallen waren, wurde nach Havanna beordert. Sechzehn Jahre lang wurde Cohiba nie kommerziell verkauft — ausschließlich als diplomatisches Geschenk an Staatsoberhäupter überreicht. Brandt, Mitterrand und Gaddafi erhielten alle Kisten dieser namenlosen Zigarre.\r\n\r\n1982 öffnete Kuba Cohiba dem internationalen Handel. Der Name stammt aus der Taíno-Sprache — der Sprache der Ureinwohner Kubas — und bedeutet Tabak. Cohiba ist heute die weltweit bekannteste, meistgefälschte und begehrteste Zigarrenmarke.\r\n\r\nDie El Laguito Fabrik, eingebettet in eine ehemalige Havannaer Villa, ist das Heiligtum der Marke. Ihre Torcedoras — überwiegend Frauen — sind Kubas bestbezahlte Zigarrenhandwerkerinnen. Eine Cohiba zu rauchen bedeutet, sechs Jahrzehnte Revolutionsgeschichte zu inhalieren.', `history_zh` = '科伊巴诞生于最高度保密之中，专为菲德尔·卡斯特罗服务。爱德华多·里维拉是一位雪茄卷制师，他精湛的个人雪茄引起了卡斯特罗警卫的注意，被召至哈瓦那。十六年间，科伊巴从未商业销售——仅作为外交礼物赠予各国元首。勃兰特、密特朗和卡扎菲都曾收到这种无名雪茄的礼盒。\r\n\r\n1982年，面对日益增长的外交需求，古巴决定向国际市场开放科伊巴。品牌名称来自泰诺语——古巴原住民的语言——意为烟草。科伊巴如今是全球最知名、最被仿冒、最令人垂涎的雪茄品牌。\r\n\r\n坐落在哈瓦那旧宅中的拉古尼托工厂是品牌的圣地。女卷制师们——主要为女性——是古巴薪酬最高的雪茄工匠。吸一支科伊巴，就是在吸入六十年的革命历史。', `history_ar` = 'وُلدت كوهيبا في سرية تامة لخدمة فيدل كاسترو. إدواردو ريفيرا، ملفِّف السيجار الذي لفت سجائره الشخصية الاستثنائية انتباه أحد حراس كاسترو، استُدعي إلى هافانا. لستة عشر عامًا، لم تُطرح كوهيبا للبيع التجاري قط — بل كانت تُقدَّم هدية دبلوماسية لرؤساء الدول. برانت وميتران والقذافي جميعهم استلموا علبًا من هذا السيجار المجهول الهوية.\r\n\r\nعام 1982، وأمام الطلب الدبلوماسي المتزايد، فتحت كوبا كوهيبا أمام التجارة الدولية. يأتي الاسم من كلمة تاينو — لغة سكان كوبا الأصليين — وتعني التبغ. تُعدّ كوهيبا اليوم العلامة التجارية الأكثر شهرةً وتقليدًا وتوقًا في عالم السيجار.\r\n\r\nمصنع إل لاغونيتو، الكامن في قصر هافاني سابق، هو حرم العلامة. ملفِّفاتها — معظمهن نساء — هن أعلى حِرفيات السيجار أجرًا في كوبا. إشعال كوهيبا يعني استنشاق ستة عقود من التاريخ الثوري.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Behike BHK\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"Launched in 2010 for the brand\'s 44th anniversary, the Behike is the rarest and most expensive vitola in Cuban history. It uses the ultra-rare medio tiempo leaf — growing at the very top of the tobacco plant, too small to harvest at scale. Three formats only, a few thousand boxes per year. Perfect scores from multiple experts. Unit price: €30–50.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"BHK 52\", \"BHK 54\", \"BHK 56\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 98, \"year\": 2011}]}, {\"name\": \"Línea 1492\", \"color\": \"#C04000\", \"story\": \"Created for the 500th anniversary of the Americas\' discovery in 1992. The Sublimes EL and Pirámides are among the house\'s rarest vitolas, available as regional editions in select countries only. The Línea 1492 embodies everyday luxury Cohiba — full body without excess.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Sublimes\", \"Pirámides\", \"Robusto Extra\", \"Coronas Especiales\"]}, {\"name\": \"Siglo I–VI\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The Clásicos — Castro\'s original range. Siglos progress from I to VI in length and intensity. The Lancero (elongated Siglo VI) remains the ultimate test for any Cuban torcedor. The gold band with its black stripe has become the universal symbol of prestige.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Siglo I\", \"Siglo II\", \"Siglo III\", \"Siglo IV\", \"Siglo V\", \"Siglo VI\"]}, {\"name\": \"Maduro 5\", \"color\": \"#3D1C00\", \"story\": \"Launched in 2007, the first Maduro in the Cuban universe. The wrapper is aged 5 additional years in barrels, creating paradoxical sweetness despite the power. Notes of prunes, dark chocolate, roasted coffee. Traditional Cuban smokers were unsettled by this unexpected softness. Now iconic.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Maduro x5\", \"vitolas\": [\"Genios\", \"Mágicos\", \"Secretos\", \"Divinos\"]}, {\"name\": \"Serie D\", \"color\": \"#5C1A00\", \"story\": \"The Robaina — Robusto format (50 x 124mm), king of formats. The Serie D No.4 is the world\'s reference Robusto. Densely packed, it releases a unique spiced complexity mid-smoke. Essential in any serious humidor.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"No.4\", \"No.5\", \"No.6\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Behike BHK\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"Lanzada en 2010 para el 44º aniversario de la marca, la Behike es la vitola más rara y costosa de la historia cubana. Utiliza la rarísima hoja medio tiempo — que crece en la cima de la planta de tabaco, demasiado pequeña para cosechar a escala. Solo tres formatos, unos pocos miles de cajas al año. Puntuaciones perfectas de múltiples expertos. Precio unitario: 30-50€.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"BHK 52\", \"BHK 54\", \"BHK 56\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 98, \"year\": 2011}]}, {\"name\": \"Línea 1492\", \"color\": \"#C04000\", \"story\": \"Creada para el 500º aniversario del descubrimiento de América en 1992. Los Sublimes EL y Pirámides están entre las vitolas más raras de la casa, disponibles solo como ediciones regionales en países seleccionados. La Línea 1492 encarna el lujo cotidiano de Cohiba — cuerpo completo sin exceso.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Sublimes\", \"Pirámides\", \"Robusto Extra\", \"Coronas Especiales\"]}, {\"name\": \"Siglo I–VI\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"Los Clásicos — la gama original de Castro. Los Siglos progresan del I al VI en longitud e intensidad. El Lancero (Siglo VI alargado) sigue siendo la prueba definitiva de todo torcedor cubano. La banda dorada con su franja negra se ha convertido en el símbolo universal del prestigio.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Siglo I\", \"Siglo II\", \"Siglo III\", \"Siglo IV\", \"Siglo V\", \"Siglo VI\"]}, {\"name\": \"Maduro 5\", \"color\": \"#3D1C00\", \"story\": \"Lanzada en 2007, la primera Maduro en el universo cubano — una revolución. La envolvente Maduro se añeja 5 años adicionales en barricas, creando una dulzura paradójica a pesar del poder. Notas de ciruela, chocolate negro, café tostado. Actualmente icónica.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Maduro x5\", \"vitolas\": [\"Genios\", \"Mágicos\", \"Secretos\", \"Divinos\"]}, {\"name\": \"Serie D\", \"color\": \"#5C1A00\", \"story\": \"El Robaina — formato Robusto (50 x 124mm), rey de los formatos. Bien apretada, libera a mitad de fumada una inesperada complejidad especiada. Imprescindible en cualquier humidor serio.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"No.4\", \"No.5\", \"No.6\"]}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Behike BHK\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"Zum 44. Jubiläum 2010 lanciert, ist die Behike die seltenste und teuerste Vitola der kubanischen Geschichte. Sie verwendet das ultrararere Medio-Tiempo-Blatt — das an der Spitze der Tabakpflanze wächst, zu klein für die Ernte. Nur drei Formate, einige tausend Kisten pro Jahr. Perfekte Bewertungen von mehreren Experten. Stückpreis: 30-50€.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"BHK 52\", \"BHK 54\", \"BHK 56\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 98, \"year\": 2011}]}, {\"name\": \"Línea 1492\", \"color\": \"#C04000\", \"story\": \"Zum 500. Jahrestag der Entdeckung Amerikas 1992 geschaffen. Die Sublimes EL und Pirámides gehören zu den seltensten Vitolas des Hauses, nur als Regionaleditionen in ausgewählten Ländern erhältlich.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Sublimes\", \"Pirámides\", \"Robusto Extra\", \"Coronas Especiales\"]}, {\"name\": \"Siglo I–VI\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"Die Clásicos — Castros ursprüngliches Sortiment. Die Siglos steigern sich von I bis VI in Länge und Intensität. Der Lancero bleibt die ultimative Prüfung für jeden kubanischen Torcedor. Das goldene Band ist zum universellen Symbol des Prestiges geworden.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Siglo I\", \"Siglo II\", \"Siglo III\", \"Siglo IV\", \"Siglo V\", \"Siglo VI\"]}, {\"name\": \"Maduro 5\", \"color\": \"#3D1C00\", \"story\": \"2007 lanciert, die erste Maduro im kubanischen Universum. Der Wrapper reift 5 Jahre zusätzlich in Fässern und schafft eine paradoxe Süße trotz der Stärke. Noten von Pflaume, dunkler Schokolade, geröstetem Kaffee. Heute ikonisch.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Maduro x5\", \"vitolas\": [\"Genios\", \"Mágicos\", \"Secretos\", \"Divinos\"]}, {\"name\": \"Serie D\", \"color\": \"#5C1A00\", \"story\": \"Das Robaina — Robusto-Format (50 x 124mm), König der Formate. Dicht gerollt, entfaltet es zur Mitte des Rauchens eine unerwartete Würzkomplexität. Unverzichtbar in jedem seriösen Humidor.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"No.4\", \"No.5\", \"No.6\"]}]', `gamme_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Behike BHK\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"2010年为品牌44周年推出，Behike是古巴历史上最稀有、最昂贵的雪茄规格。使用极为罕见的中段叶（medio tiempo）——生长在烟草植株的顶端，数量太少无法大规模采收。仅三种规格，每年仅数千盒。多位专家给予满分评价。单价：30-50欧元。\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"BHK 52\", \"BHK 54\", \"BHK 56\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 98, \"year\": 2011}]}, {\"name\": \"Línea 1492\", \"color\": \"#C04000\", \"story\": \"为纪念1992年美洲发现500周年而创。Sublimes EL和Pirámides是该品牌最稀有的规格之一，仅在特定国家作为地区版供应。Línea 1492体现了科伊巴的日常奢华——饱满而不过度。\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Sublimes\", \"Pirámides\", \"Robusto Extra\", \"Coronas Especiales\"]}, {\"name\": \"Siglo I–VI\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"经典系列——卡斯特罗的原始产品线。Siglos从I到VI递增，长度与强度逐步提升。Lancero（加长版Siglo VI）是每位古巴卷制师的终极考验。金色带饰已成为威望的普世象征。\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Siglo I\", \"Siglo II\", \"Siglo III\", \"Siglo IV\", \"Siglo V\", \"Siglo VI\"]}, {\"name\": \"Maduro 5\", \"color\": \"#3D1C00\", \"story\": \"2007年推出，古巴雪茄界首款Maduro——一场革命。茄衣在桶中额外陈化5年，创造出矛盾的甜美感，尽管劲道十足。李子、黑巧克力、烘焙咖啡的风味。如今已成经典。\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Maduro x5\", \"vitolas\": [\"Genios\", \"Mágicos\", \"Secretos\", \"Divinos\"]}, {\"name\": \"Serie D\", \"color\": \"#5C1A00\", \"story\": \"罗巴伊纳——Robusto规格（50×124mm），规格之王。密实填充，在中段释放出意想不到的辛香复杂性。任何认真的雪茄收藏都不可或缺。\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"No.4\", \"No.5\", \"No.6\"]}]', `gamme_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Behike BHK\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"أُطلقت عام 2010 للاحتفال بالذكرى الرابعة والأربعين للعلامة، تُعدّ Behike أندر وأغلى سيجار في التاريخ الكوبي. تستخدم ورقة الميديو تيمبو النادرة للغاية — التي تنمو في قمة نبتة التبغ، صغيرة جدًا لا تُحصد على نطاق واسع. ثلاثة مقاسات فحسب، بضعة آلاف علبة سنويًا. تقييمات مثالية من خبراء متعددين. سعر الوحدة: 30-50 يورو.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"BHK 52\", \"BHK 54\", \"BHK 56\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 98, \"year\": 2011}]}, {\"name\": \"Línea 1492\", \"color\": \"#C04000\", \"story\": \"ابتُكرت بمناسبة الذكرى الخمسمئة لاكتشاف الأمريكتين عام 1992. السوبليمس EL والبيراميدس من أندر مقاسات الدار، متوفرة فقط كإصدارات إقليمية في دول محددة.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Sublimes\", \"Pirámides\", \"Robusto Extra\", \"Coronas Especiales\"]}, {\"name\": \"Siglo I–VI\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"الكلاسيكيات — التشكيلة الأصلية لكاسترو. تتصاعد السيغلو من الأول إلى السادس طولًا وكثافةً. يظل اللانسيرو الاختبار الأقصى لكل ملفِّف كوبي. الشريط الذهبي مع خطه الأسود أصبح الرمز العالمي للمكانة.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Siglo I\", \"Siglo II\", \"Siglo III\", \"Siglo IV\", \"Siglo V\", \"Siglo VI\"]}, {\"name\": \"Maduro 5\", \"color\": \"#3D1C00\", \"story\": \"أُطلقت عام 2007، أول مادورو في الكون الكوبي — ثورة حقيقية. تُعتَّق الغلافة خمس سنوات إضافية في البراميل، مُنتِجةً حلاوة متناقضة رغم القوة. نكهات البرقوق والشوكولاتة الداكنة والقهوة المحمَّصة. باتت أيقونية اليوم.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Maduro x5\", \"vitolas\": [\"Genios\", \"Mágicos\", \"Secretos\", \"Divinos\"]}, {\"name\": \"Serie D\", \"color\": \"#5C1A00\", \"story\": \"الروباينا — مقاس روبوستو (50 × 124 ملم)، ملك المقاسات. مضغوطة بإحكام، تُطلق في منتصف التدخين تعقيدًا توابليًا غير متوقع. لا غنى عنها في أي مجموعة جادة.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"No.4\", \"No.5\", \"No.6\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Fidel Castro\", \"anecdote\": \"Castro smoked 20–25 Cohiba cigars a day before quitting in 1985 on medical advice. He reportedly said: \'The best thing I did for my health was quit smoking. The best thing I did for my enemies was keep offering it to them.\'\"}, {\"name\": \"Jack Nicholson\", \"anecdote\": \"A notorious Cohiba Esplendidos smoker at his Oscar appearances, Nicholson helped popularize the brand in the United States despite the embargo.\"}, {\"name\": \"Che Guevara\", \"anecdote\": \"An iconic figure of the Cuban cigar, often photographed with a Cohiba. The image has become a global cultural symbol.\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Fidel Castro\", \"anecdote\": \"Castro fumaba 20–25 Cohiba cigarros al día antes de dejarlo en 1985 por consejo médico. Supuestamente dijo: \'The best thing I did for my health was quit smoking. The best thing I did for my enemies was keep offering it to them.\'\"}, {\"name\": \"Jack Nicholson\", \"anecdote\": \"A notorious Cohiba Esplendidos smoker at his Oscar appearances, Nicholson helped popularize the brand in the United States despite the embargo.\"}, {\"name\": \"Che Guevara\", \"anecdote\": \"An iconic figure of the Cuban cigar, often photographed with a Cohiba. The image has become a global cultural symbol.\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Fidel Castro\", \"anecdote\": \"Castro rauchte 20–25 Cohiba Zigarren täglich bevor er 1985 auf ärztlichen Rat aufhörte. Er soll gesagt haben: \'The best thing I did for my health was quit smoking. The best thing I did for my enemies was keep offering it to them.\'\"}, {\"name\": \"Jack Nicholson\", \"anecdote\": \"A notorious Cohiba Esplendidos smoker at his Oscar appearances, Nicholson helped popularize the brand in the United States despite the embargo.\"}, {\"name\": \"Che Guevara\", \"anecdote\": \"An iconic figure of the Cuban cigar, often photographed with a Cohiba. The image has become a global cultural symbol.\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Fidel Castro\", \"anecdote\": \"Castro 每天抽20至25支科伊巴雪茄 在1985年遵医嘱戒烟之前. 据报道他曾说： \'The best thing I did for my health was quit smoking. The best thing I did for my enemies was keep offering it to them.\'\"}, {\"name\": \"Jack Nicholson\", \"anecdote\": \"A notorious Cohiba Esplendidos smoker at his Oscar appearances, Nicholson helped popularize the brand in the United States despite the embargo.\"}, {\"name\": \"Che Guevara\", \"anecdote\": \"An iconic figure of the Cuban cigar, often photographed with a Cohiba. The image has become a global cultural symbol.\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Fidel Castro\", \"anecdote\": \"Castro كان يدخن من 20 إلى 25 سيجارة كوهيبا يوميًا قبل إقلاعه عام 1985 بنصيحة طبية. يُروى أنه قال: \'The best thing I did for my health was quit smoking. The best thing I did for my enemies was keep offering it to them.\'\"}, {\"name\": \"Jack Nicholson\", \"anecdote\": \"A notorious Cohiba Esplendidos smoker at his Oscar appearances, Nicholson helped popularize the brand in the United States despite the embargo.\"}, {\"name\": \"Che Guevara\", \"anecdote\": \"An iconic figure of the Cuban cigar, often photographed with a Cohiba. The image has become a global cultural symbol.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Spirits\", \"name\": \"Hennessy XO Cognac\", \"notes\": \"The roundness of cognac amplifies the woody notes of the Behike. A classic pairing for great occasions.\"}, {\"type\": \"Rum\", \"name\": \"Ron Santiago de Cuba 12 years\", \"notes\": \"The natural pairing — both products share the same Cuban soil. Notes of cane and tobacco in resonance.\"}, {\"type\": \"Coffee\", \"name\": \"Cuban cortadito\", \"notes\": \"The gentle bitterness of Cuban coffee perfectly supports the spiced complexity of a Siglo III after dinner.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\": \"Licores\", \"name\": \"Hennessy XO Cognac\", \"notes\": \"La redondez del coñac amplifica las notas maderosas of the Behike. Un maridaje clásico para grandes ocasiones.\"}, {\"type\": \"Ron\", \"name\": \"Ron Santiago de Cuba 12 years\", \"notes\": \"El maridaje natural — ambos productos comparten el mismo Cuban soil. Notas de cane and tobacco in resonance.\"}, {\"type\": \"Café\", \"name\": \"Cuban cortadito\", \"notes\": \"The gentle bitterness of Cuban coffee perfectly supports the spiced complexity of a Siglo III after dinner.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\": \"Spirituosen\", \"name\": \"Hennessy XO Cognac\", \"notes\": \"Die Fülle des Cognacs verstärkt die Holznoten of the Behike. Eine klassische Paarung für besondere Anlässe.\"}, {\"type\": \"Rum\", \"name\": \"Ron Santiago de Cuba 12 years\", \"notes\": \"Die natürliche Paarung — beide Produkte teilen denselben Cuban soil. Noten von cane and tobacco in resonance.\"}, {\"type\": \"Kaffee\", \"name\": \"Cuban cortadito\", \"notes\": \"The gentle bitterness of Cuban coffee perfectly supports the spiced complexity of a Siglo III after dinner.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\": \"烈酒\", \"name\": \"Hennessy XO Cognac\", \"notes\": \"干邑的圆润感放大了木质气息 of the Behike. 盛大场合的经典搭配.\"}, {\"type\": \"朗姆酒\", \"name\": \"Ron Santiago de Cuba 12 years\", \"notes\": \"天然的搭配 — 两种产品共享相同的 Cuban soil. 风味： cane and tobacco in resonance.\"}, {\"type\": \"咖啡\", \"name\": \"Cuban cortadito\", \"notes\": \"The gentle bitterness of Cuban coffee perfectly supports the spiced complexity of a Siglo III after dinner.\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\": \"المسكرات\", \"name\": \"Hennessy XO Cognac\", \"notes\": \"نعومة الكونياك تُضخِّم النكهات الخشبية of the Behike. مقارنة كلاسيكية للمناسبات الكبرى.\"}, {\"type\": \"الروم\", \"name\": \"Ron Santiago de Cuba 12 years\", \"notes\": \"المقارنة الطبيعية — كلا المنتجين يشتركان في نفس Cuban soil. نكهات: cane and tobacco in resonance.\"}, {\"type\": \"القهوة\", \"name\": \"Cuban cortadito\", \"notes\": \"The gentle bitterness of Cuban coffee perfectly supports the spiced complexity of a Siglo III after dinner.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Cohiba';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'Cohiba USA is one of the most complex intellectual property stories in the tobacco industry — a forty-year legal battle involving two governments, millions of dollars in attorney fees, and a name that two companies each legitimately claim under different legal systems.\r\n\r\nGeneral Cigar Company registered the Cohiba trademark in the United States in 1978, several years before Habanos S.A. pursued its own American registration. The US trade embargo against Cuba — in effect since 1962 — rendered the Cuban brand legally nonexistent on American soil. General Cigar seized this opportunity and created its own Cohiba range for the American market, manufactured in the Dominican Republic.\r\n\r\nHabanos S.A. challenged this appropriation starting in the 1990s. American courts rendered contradictory decisions across jurisdictions and years. In 2004, a ruling favorable to General Cigar confirmed their right to market Cohiba in the US. In 2007, an appeal partially reversed this decision. The case is one of the longest and most complex in the history of American trademark law.\r\n\r\nThe practical result: the United States is the only market in the world where two entirely different brands carry the name Cohiba. General Cigar\'s American version uses Dominican and Honduran tobacco. Its profile — softer, more accessible, focused on consistency — differs radically from the Cuban version. Both coexist legally and commercially, to the lasting confusion of uninformed enthusiasts.', `history_es` = 'Cohiba USA es una de las historias de propiedad intelectual más complejas de la industria del tabaco: una batalla judicial de cuarenta años en la que intervienen dos gobiernos, millones de dólares en honorarios de abogados y un nombre que dos empresas reivindican legítimamente, cada una según un sistema jurídico distinto.\n\nGeneral Cigar Company registró la marca Cohiba en Estados Unidos en 1978, varios años antes de que Habanos S.A. iniciara sus propios trámites de registro estadounidense. El embargo comercial estadounidense contra Cuba —vigente desde 1962— hacía que la marca cubana fuera legalmente inexistente en suelo estadounidense. General Cigar aprovechó la oportunidad y creó su propia gama Cohiba para el mercado estadounidense, fabricada en la República Dominicana.\n\nHabanos S.A. impugnó esa apropiación a partir de los años noventa. Los tribunales estadounidenses dictaron resoluciones contradictorias según la jurisdicción y el año. En 2004, una sentencia favorable a General Cigar confirmó su derecho a comercializar Cohiba en Estados Unidos. En 2007, una apelación revocó parcialmente esa decisión. El expediente es uno de los más largos y complejos de la historia del derecho de marcas estadounidense.\n\nEl resultado práctico: Estados Unidos es el único mercado del mundo donde dos marcas completamente distintas llevan el nombre Cohiba. La versión estadounidense de General Cigar emplea tabaco dominicano y hondureño. Su perfil —más suave, más accesible, centrado en la regularidad— difiere radicalmente de la versión cubana. Ambas conviven legal y comercialmente desde hace décadas, para confusión duradera de los aficionados no avisados.', `history_de` = 'Cohiba USA ist eine der verwickeltsten Geschichten des geistigen Eigentums in der Tabakindustrie — ein vierzigjähriger Rechtsstreit, in dem zwei Regierungen, Anwaltshonorare in Millionenhöhe und ein Name auftreten, den zwei Unternehmen nach je unterschiedlichen Rechtsordnungen zu Recht für sich beanspruchen.\n\nDie General Cigar Company ließ die Marke Cohiba 1978 in den Vereinigten Staaten eintragen, mehrere Jahre bevor Habanos S.A. eine eigene amerikanische Anmeldung betrieb. Das seit 1962 geltende US-Handelsembargo gegen Kuba machte die kubanische Marke auf amerikanischem Boden rechtlich nicht existent. General Cigar ergriff diese Gelegenheit und schuf eine eigene Cohiba-Linie für den amerikanischen Markt, hergestellt in der Dominikanischen Republik.\n\nAb den 1990er Jahren focht Habanos S.A. diese Aneignung an. Die amerikanischen Gerichte entschieden je nach Gerichtsbarkeit und Jahr widersprüchlich. 2004 bestätigte ein für General Cigar günstiges Urteil deren Recht, Cohiba in den Vereinigten Staaten zu vertreiben. 2007 hob ein Berufungsverfahren diese Entscheidung teilweise auf. Der Fall gehört zu den längsten und verwickeltsten der amerikanischen Markenrechtsgeschichte.\n\nDas praktische Ergebnis: Die Vereinigten Staaten sind der einzige Markt der Welt, auf dem zwei völlig verschiedene Marken den Namen Cohiba tragen. Die amerikanische Version von General Cigar verwendet dominikanischen und honduranischen Tabak. Ihr Profil — milder, zugänglicher, auf Gleichmäßigkeit ausgerichtet — unterscheidet sich grundlegend von der kubanischen Version. Beide bestehen seit Jahrzehnten rechtlich und kommerziell nebeneinander, zur anhaltenden Verwirrung nicht eingeweihter Liebhaber.', `history_zh` = 'Cohiba USA 是烟草业中最错综复杂的知识产权故事之一——一场长达四十年的法律战，牵涉两国政府、数百万美元的律师费，以及一个被两家企业依据不同法律体系各自合法主张的名字。\n\nGeneral Cigar 公司于 1978 年在美国注册了 Cohiba 商标，比 Habanos S.A. 着手办理自己的美国注册手续早了数年。自 1962 年起生效的美国对古巴贸易禁运，使这个古巴品牌在美国境内于法律上并不存在。General Cigar 抓住这一机会，为美国市场创立了自己的 Cohiba 系列，在多米尼加共和国生产。\n\nHabanos S.A. 从 1990 年代起对这一占用提出异议。美国法院因管辖法院和年份不同而作出相互矛盾的判决。2004 年，一项有利于 General Cigar 的判决确认了其在美国销售 Cohiba 的权利；2007 年，一次上诉又部分推翻了该判决。此案是美国商标法史上历时最久、纠葛最深的案件之一。\n\n实际结果是：美国是全世界唯一一个由两个截然不同的品牌共用 Cohiba 之名的市场。General Cigar 的美国版使用多米尼加与洪都拉斯烟叶，其风格更柔和、更易入口、以稳定一致见长，与古巴版大相径庭。两者在法律与商业上并存了数十年，也让不明就里的爱好者长期困惑。', `history_ar` = 'تُعدّ Cohiba USA واحدة من أعقد قصص الملكية الفكرية في صناعة التبغ: معركة قضائية دامت أربعين عاماً، تتقاطع فيها حكومتان وملايين الدولارات من أتعاب المحامين واسمٌ تطالب به شركتان، كلٌّ منهما محقّة وفق نظام قانوني مختلف.\n\nسجّلت شركة General Cigar علامة Cohiba في الولايات المتحدة عام 1978، قبل سنوات من شروع Habanos S.A. في إجراءات تسجيلها الأمريكية الخاصة. وكان الحظر التجاري الأمريكي على كوبا — الساري منذ 1962 — يجعل العلامة الكوبية معدومة قانونياً على الأراضي الأمريكية. فاغتنمت General Cigar الفرصة وأنشأت تشكيلة Cohiba خاصة بها للسوق الأمريكية، تُصنع في جمهورية الدومينيكان.\n\nاعترضت Habanos S.A. على هذا الاستيلاء ابتداءً من التسعينيات. وأصدرت المحاكم الأمريكية أحكاماً متناقضة باختلاف الولايات القضائية والسنوات. ففي 2004 أكّد حكم لصالح General Cigar حقّها في تسويق Cohiba في الولايات المتحدة، وفي 2007 نقض الاستئناف ذلك الحكم جزئياً. والملف من أطول ملفات تاريخ قانون العلامات التجارية الأمريكي وأشدّها تعقيداً.\n\nأما النتيجة العملية فهي أن الولايات المتحدة هي السوق الوحيدة في العالم التي تحمل فيها علامتان مختلفتان تماماً اسم Cohiba. النسخة الأمريكية من General Cigar تستخدم تبغاً دومينيكياً وهندوراسياً، وطابعها — أنعم وأيسر تناولاً وقائم على الانتظام — يختلف جذرياً عن النسخة الكوبية. وتتعايش النسختان قانونياً وتجارياً منذ عقود، في التباس دائم لدى الهواة غير المطّلعين.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Cohiba Blue\", \"color\": \"#1A3A6B\", \"story\": \"Entry-level range — Dominican Connecticut wrapper on a Honduran-Dominican blend. Light and creamy profile, built for the American daily market. No flavor relationship to the Cuban range despite the identical name.\"}, {\"name\": \"Cohiba Red Dot\", \"color\": \"#8B0000\", \"story\": \"The American premium range with Dominican Piloto Cubano wrapper. More body, cedar and soft spice notes. The Red Dot was for years the default prestige cigar of American steakhouses through the 1990s-2010s.\"}, {\"name\": \"Cohiba Macassar\", \"color\": \"#2C1A0E\", \"story\": \"The high-end American range using Cameroonian, Nicaraguan, and Dominican tobacco. Created to challenge the Cuban brand\'s quality reputation. Powerful profile, deep woody and spiced notes.\"}, {\"name\": \"Cohiba Nicaragua\", \"color\": \"#3D5C1A\", \"story\": \"The newest range, 100% Nicaraguan. Implicitly acknowledges that Nicaragua has surpassed the Dominican Republic in terms of intensity and complexity for the American premium market.\"}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\":\"Cohiba Blue\",\"color\":\"#1A3A6B\",\"story\":\"Gama de entrada: capa Dominican Connecticut sobre ligada hondureño-dominicana. Perfil ligero y cremoso, pensado para el consumo diario estadounidense. Ninguna relación de sabor con la gama cubana pese al nombre idéntico.\"},{\"name\":\"Cohiba Red Dot\",\"color\":\"#8B0000\",\"story\":\"La gama premium estadounidense, con capa Dominican Piloto Cubano. Más cuerpo, notas de cedro y especias dulces. El Red Dot fue durante mucho tiempo el puro de prestigio por defecto de los steakhouses estadounidenses entre 1990 y 2010.\"},{\"name\":\"Cohiba Macassar\",\"color\":\"#2C1A0E\",\"story\":\"Gama alta con tabaco camerunés, nicaragüense y dominicano. Creada para disputar la reputación cubana. Perfil potente, notas amaderadas y especiadas profundas: la versión estadounidense más ambiciosa.\"},{\"name\":\"Cohiba Nicaragua\",\"color\":\"#3D5C1A\",\"story\":\"La más reciente de las gamas, 100 % nicaragüense. Reconoce de forma implícita que Nicaragua ha superado a la República Dominicana en intensidad y complejidad en el mercado estadounidense de las dos últimas décadas.\"}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\":\"Cohiba Blue\",\"color\":\"#1A3A6B\",\"story\":\"Einstiegslinie — Dominican-Connecticut-Deckblatt auf honduranisch-dominikanischer Mischung. Leichtes, cremiges Profil, für den amerikanischen Alltag gebaut. Trotz des gleichen Namens keinerlei geschmackliche Verwandtschaft mit der kubanischen Linie.\"},{\"name\":\"Cohiba Red Dot\",\"color\":\"#8B0000\",\"story\":\"Die amerikanische Premiumlinie mit Deckblatt Dominican Piloto Cubano. Mehr Körper, Noten von Zedernholz und milden Gewürzen. Der Red Dot war lange die selbstverständliche Prestigezigarre der amerikanischen Steakhäuser der Jahre 1990 bis 2010.\"},{\"name\":\"Cohiba Macassar\",\"color\":\"#2C1A0E\",\"story\":\"Spitzenlinie mit kamerunischem, nicaraguanischem und dominikanischem Tabak. Geschaffen, um dem kubanischen Ruf entgegenzutreten. Kräftiges Profil, tiefe Holz- und Gewürznoten — die ehrgeizigste amerikanische Version.\"},{\"name\":\"Cohiba Nicaragua\",\"color\":\"#3D5C1A\",\"story\":\"Die jüngste der Linien, zu 100 % nicaraguanisch. Sie räumt stillschweigend ein, dass Nicaragua die Dominikanische Republik in den letzten zwei Jahrzehnten auf dem amerikanischen Markt an Intensität und Komplexität überholt hat.\"}]', `gamme_zh` = '[{\"name\":\"Cohiba Blue\",\"color\":\"#1A3A6B\",\"story\":\"入门系列——Dominican Connecticut 茄衣，配洪都拉斯与多米尼加填充。风格轻盈奶润，为美国日常市场而生。尽管同名，与古巴系列在风味上毫无关系。\"},{\"name\":\"Cohiba Red Dot\",\"color\":\"#8B0000\",\"story\":\"美国高端系列，采用 Dominican Piloto Cubano 茄衣。酒体更饱满，带雪松与甜香料气息。1990 至 2010 年间，Red Dot 长期是美国牛排馆里默认的体面之选。\"},{\"name\":\"Cohiba Macassar\",\"color\":\"#2C1A0E\",\"story\":\"顶级系列，选用喀麦隆、尼加拉瓜与多米尼加烟叶。为挑战古巴的声望而生。风格强劲，木质与香料气息深沉——美国版中最具野心的一支。\"},{\"name\":\"Cohiba Nicaragua\",\"color\":\"#3D5C1A\",\"story\":\"最新的一条产品线，百分之百尼加拉瓜配方。它等于默认：过去二十年间，在美国市场的强度与复杂度上，尼加拉瓜已经超过了多米尼加共和国。\"}]', `gamme_ar` = '[{\"name\":\"Cohiba Blue\",\"color\":\"#1A3A6B\",\"story\":\"تشكيلة المدخل — غلاف Dominican Connecticut على خلطة هندوراسية دومينيكية. طابع خفيف وكريمي، مصمَّم للاستهلاك اليومي في السوق الأمريكية. ولا صلة في المذاق بالتشكيلة الكوبية رغم تطابق الاسم.\"},{\"name\":\"Cohiba Red Dot\",\"color\":\"#8B0000\",\"story\":\"التشكيلة الفاخرة الأمريكية بغلاف Dominican Piloto Cubano. جسم أوفر، ولمسات من الأرز والتوابل الحلوة. وظلّ Red Dot طويلاً سيجار الوجاهة البديهي في مطاعم الشرائح الأمريكية بين 1990 و2010.\"},{\"name\":\"Cohiba Macassar\",\"color\":\"#2C1A0E\",\"story\":\"التشكيلة العليا بتبغ كاميروني ونيكاراغوي ودومينيكي، أُنشئت لمنازلة السمعة الكوبية. طابع قوي بلمسات خشبية وتوابل عميقة — وهي أطمح النسخ الأمريكية.\"},{\"name\":\"Cohiba Nicaragua\",\"color\":\"#3D5C1A\",\"story\":\"أحدث التشكيلات، نيكاراغوية مئة بالمئة. وتقرّ ضمناً بأن نيكاراغوا تجاوزت جمهورية الدومينيكان في الشدّة والتعقيد داخل السوق الأمريكية خلال العقدين الأخيرين.\"}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"The Cohiba legal battle\", \"anecdote\": \"The Cohiba case (General Cigar vs. Habanos S.A.) is cited in American trademark law textbooks as a paradigmatic example of transnational brand conflicts in the context of trade embargoes. It lasted over 20 years, involved three separate federal courts, and remains without a definitive resolution.\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\":\"Batalla judicial Cohiba\",\"anecdote\":\"El caso Cohiba (General Cigar contra Habanos S.A.) se cita en los manuales de derecho estadounidense como ejemplo paradigmático de conflicto de marcas transnacionales en contexto de embargo. Duró más de veinte años, implicó a tres tribunales federales distintos y todavía no está definitivamente cerrado.\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\":\"Rechtsstreit um Cohiba\",\"anecdote\":\"Der Fall Cohiba (General Cigar gegen Habanos S.A.) wird in amerikanischen Rechtslehrbüchern als Musterfall transnationaler Markenkonflikte unter Embargobedingungen geführt. Er dauerte über zwanzig Jahre, betraf drei verschiedene Bundesgerichte und ist bis heute nicht endgültig abgeschlossen.\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\":\"高希霸商标诉讼\",\"anecdote\":\"高希霸案（General Cigar 诉 Habanos S.A.）被美国法学教材列为禁运背景下跨国商标冲突的典型案例。该案历时二十余年，先后涉及三个不同的联邦法院，至今仍未彻底了结。\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\":\"المعركة القضائية حول كوهيبا\",\"anecdote\":\"تُدرَّس قضية كوهيبا (جنرال سيغار ضد هابانوس ش.م.) في كتب القانون الأمريكية كنموذج للنزاعات العابرة للحدود على العلامات التجارية في ظل الحصار. استمرّت أكثر من عشرين عامًا، وشملت ثلاث محاكم فيدرالية مختلفة، ولم تُحسَم نهائيًا بعد.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Spirits\", \"name\": \"Maker\'s Mark Bourbon\", \"notes\": \"The authentic American pairing for the Red Dot. The vanilla and caramel of Kentucky bourbon amplify the sweetness of the Dominican wrapper without overwhelming the modest profile.\"}, {\"type\": \"Beer\", \"name\": \"Pacific Northwest IPA\", \"notes\": \"For the Cohiba Blue, the floral bitterness of a late-hopped IPA offers an interesting contrast with the creamy lightness of the Connecticut wrapper.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\":\"Destilado\",\"name\":\"Bourbon Maker\'s Mark\",\"notes\":\"El maridaje estadounidense auténtico para el Red Dot. La vainilla y el caramelo del bourbon de Kentucky amplifican el dulzor de la capa dominicana sin aplastar su perfil modesto.\"},{\"type\":\"Cerveza\",\"name\":\"IPA del Pacific Northwest\",\"notes\":\"Para el Cohiba Blue, el amargor floral de una IPA con lupulado tardío ofrece un contraste interesante con la ligereza cremosa de la capa Connecticut.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\":\"Spirituose\",\"name\":\"Bourbon Maker\'s Mark\",\"notes\":\"Die authentisch amerikanische Kombination für die Red Dot. Vanille und Karamell des Kentucky-Bourbons verstärken die Süße des dominikanischen Deckblatts, ohne dessen zurückhaltendes Profil zu überdecken.\"},{\"type\":\"Bier\",\"name\":\"IPA aus dem Pacific Northwest\",\"notes\":\"Für die Cohiba Blue bietet die blumige Bittere eines spät gehopften IPA einen reizvollen Kontrast zur cremigen Leichtigkeit des Connecticut-Deckblatts.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\":\"烈酒\",\"name\":\"Maker\'s Mark 波本\",\"notes\":\"这是 Red Dot 最地道的美式搭配。肯塔基波本的香草与焦糖放大多米尼加茄衣的甜润，却不压过它谦和的本色。\"},{\"type\":\"啤酒\",\"name\":\"太平洋西北 IPA\",\"notes\":\"对高希霸 Blue 而言，后段投花 IPA 的花香苦韵，与康涅狄格茄衣的奶油般轻盈形成有趣反差。\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\":\"مشروب روحي\",\"name\":\"بوربون ميكرز مارك\",\"notes\":\"المزاوجة الأمريكية الأصيلة لـ«ريد دوت». الفانيلا والكراميل في بوربون كنتاكي يُبرزان حلاوة الغلاف الدومينيكي دون أن يطغيا على طابعه المتحفّظ.\"},{\"type\":\"بيرة\",\"name\":\"آي بي إيه من شمال غرب المحيط الهادئ\",\"notes\":\"مع «كوهيبا بلو»، تمنح المرارة الزهرية لبيرة آي بي إيه المُضاف إليها الجنجل متأخرًا تباينًا لافتًا مع الخفّة الكريمية لغلاف كونيتيكت.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Cohiba USA';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'Gerhard Dannemann arrived in Brazil in 1873 at the age of 23, one of thousands of German immigrants who had settled in the southern Brazilian states during the nineteenth century. Unlike most who came for agriculture or light industry, Dannemann was drawn specifically to tobacco — he had knowledge of the trade from his German background, and the tobacco he encountered in Bahia\'s Recôncavo basin was unlike anything he had expected.\r\n\r\nBahian tobacco has been cultivated in the fertile valleys south of the Rio Paraguaçu since the seventeenth century, originally by enslaved African labor under Portuguese colonial administration. The soil there — dark, alluvial, rich in organic matter from centuries of flooding and deposit — produces a leaf of natural softness and mild sweetness that bears no resemblance to the aggressive character of Cuban tobacco or the peppery intensity of Nicaraguan. It is closer in profile to good Indonesian Sumatra than to any Caribbean variety: gentle, slightly spiced, with a finish of cashew and honey that makes it uniquely suitable for accessible cigar formats.\r\n\r\nDannemann recognized the commercial potential of Bahian tobacco for the European market at a moment when the German middle class was developing a taste for small cigars and cigarillos as an affordable daily habit. He founded his factory in São Félix da Cachoeira — a colonial town directly across the Rio Paraguaçu from the larger market of Cachoeira — and spent his first decade establishing both his tobacco sourcing and his European distribution relationships.\r\n\r\nThe operation has remained in São Félix for 150 years. The colonial warehouse that Dannemann converted in 1873 has been expanded and updated but never relocated. The company passed through the Dannemann family for four generations before its acquisition by the Swisher International group — but the production location, the tobacco sourcing from surrounding Bahian farms, and the fundamental proposition of the product have remained constant. Dannemann cigarillos are one of the few luxury consumer products whose manufacturing context has genuinely not moved in a century and a half.', `history_es` = 'Gerhard Dannemann llegó de Alemania en 1873 a São Félix da Cachoeira, Bahia, Brasil. Descubrió el suave tabaco bahiano y fundó su fábrica junto al río Paraguaçu. 150 años después, la misma fábrica produce en São Félix. Dannemann es el fabricante de cigarros más antiguo de las Américas aún en funcionamiento.', `history_de` = 'Gerhard Dannemann kam 1873 aus Deutschland nach São Félix da Cachoeira, Bahia, Brasilien. Er entdeckte den sanften bahianischen Tabak und gründete seine Fabrik am Fluss Paraguaçu. 150 Jahre später produziert dieselbe Fabrik noch in São Félix. Dannemann ist der älteste Zigarrenhersteller Amerikas, der noch in Betrieb ist.', `history_zh` = '格哈德·丹纳曼于1873年从德国来到巴西巴伊亚州圣费利克斯达卡舒埃拉。他发现了柔和的巴伊亚烟草，并在帕拉圭苏河边建立了工厂。150年后，同一家工厂仍在圣费利克斯生产。丹纳曼是美洲仍在运营的最古老雪茄制造商。', `history_ar` = 'وصل غيرهارد دانيمان من ألمانيا عام 1873 إلى ساو فيليكس دا كاشويرا في باهيا، البرازيل. اكتشف التبغ الباهياني الناعم وأسّس مصنعه على ضفاف نهر باراغواسو. بعد 150 عامًا، المصنع ذاته لا يزال ينتج في ساو فيليكس. دانيمان أقدم مصنع سيجار في الأمريكتين لا يزال يعمل.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Dannemann Speciale\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The flagship product — cigarillo with Bahia wrapper. Sweet notes of honey, cashew, light cedar. Short format (34 x 112mm), 15 minutes. The Brazilian cigar the whole world knows — smoked from São Paulo to Amsterdam and the Paris Marais district.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Brazilian Bahia\", \"vitolas\": [\"Speciale\", \"Brasil\", \"Moods\"]}, {\"name\": \"Dannemann Pierrot\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Mini format, 10 minutes. Vanilla or cherry flavoring. The Brazilian recreational cigar — convivial, unpretentious, festive. Smoked at Rio carnivals and football matches for 50 years.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Brazilian Bahia\", \"vitolas\": [\"Pierrot\", \"Pierrot Vanilla\", \"Pierrot Cherry\"]}, {\"name\": \"Dannemann Premium\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"The serious side of Dannemann — full-length cigars, 2-year-aged Bahia tobacco. More complex notes than the standard ranges: vanilla, cashew, light cinnamon spice. Robusto and Toro formats. The discovery for enthusiasts who knew Dannemann only from the cigarillos.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Brazilian Bahia\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Corona\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Dannemann Speciale\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The flagship product — cigarillo with Bahia wrapper. Sweet notas de miel, cashew, light cedro. Short format (34 x 112mm), 15 minutes. The Brazilian cigar the whole world knows — smoked from São Paulo to Amsterdam and the Paris Marais district.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Brazilian Bahia\", \"vitolas\": [\"Speciale\", \"Brasil\", \"Moods\"]}, {\"name\": \"Dannemann Pierrot\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Mini format, 10 minutes. Vanilla or cherry flavoring. The Brazilian recreational cigar — convivial, unpretentious, festive. Smoked at Rio carnivals and football matches for 50 years.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Brazilian Bahia\", \"vitolas\": [\"Pierrot\", \"Pierrot Vanilla\", \"Pierrot Cherry\"]}, {\"name\": \"Dannemann Premium\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"The serious side of Dannemann — full-length cigars, 2-year-aged Bahia tobacco. More complex notes than the standard ranges: vainilla, cashew, light canela spice. Robusto and Toro formats. The discovery for aficionados who knew Dannemann only from the cigarillos.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Brazilian Bahia\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Corona\"]}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Dannemann Speciale\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The flagship product — cigarillo with Bahia wrapper. Sweet Noten von honey, cashew, light Zeder. Short format (34 x 112mm), 15 minutes. The Brazilian cigar the whole world knows — smoked from São Paulo to Amsterdam and the Paris Marais district.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Brazilian Bahia\", \"vitolas\": [\"Speciale\", \"Brasil\", \"Moods\"]}, {\"name\": \"Dannemann Pierrot\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Mini format, 10 minutes. Vanilla or cherry flavoring. The Brazilian recreational cigar — convivial, unpretentious, festive. Smoked at Rio carnivals and football matches for 50 years.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Brazilian Bahia\", \"vitolas\": [\"Pierrot\", \"Pierrot Vanilla\", \"Pierrot Cherry\"]}, {\"name\": \"Dannemann Premium\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"The serious side of Dannemann — full-length cigars, 2-year-aged Bahia tobacco. More complex notes than the standard ranges: Vanille, cashew, light cinnamon spice. Robusto and Toro formats. The discovery for enthusiasts who knew Dannemann only from the cigarillos.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Brazilian Bahia\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Corona\"]}]', `gamme_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Dannemann Speciale\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The flagship product — cigarillo with Bahia wrapper. Sweet 风味包括： honey, cashew, light 雪松木. Short format (34 x 112mm), 15 分钟. The Brazilian cigar the whole world knows — smoked from São Paulo to Amsterdam and the Paris Marais district.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Brazilian Bahia\", \"vitolas\": [\"Speciale\", \"Brasil\", \"Moods\"]}, {\"name\": \"Dannemann Pierrot\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Mini format, 10 分钟. Vanilla or cherry flavoring. The Brazilian recreational cigar — convivial, unpretentious, festive. Smoked at Rio carnivals and football matches for 50 years.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Brazilian Bahia\", \"vitolas\": [\"Pierrot\", \"Pierrot Vanilla\", \"Pierrot Cherry\"]}, {\"name\": \"Dannemann Premium\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"The serious side of Dannemann — full-length cigars, 2-year-aged Bahia tobacco. More complex notes than the standard ranges: 香草, cashew, light 肉桂 spice. Robusto and Toro formats. The discovery for 爱好者 who knew Dannemann only from the cigarillos.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Brazilian Bahia\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Corona\"]}]', `gamme_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Dannemann Speciale\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The flagship product — cigarillo with Bahia wrapper. Sweet نكهات:  honey, cashew, light أرز. Short format (34 x 112mm), 15 دقيقة. The Brazilian cigar the whole world knows — smoked from São Paulo to Amsterdam and the Paris Marais district.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Brazilian Bahia\", \"vitolas\": [\"Speciale\", \"Brasil\", \"Moods\"]}, {\"name\": \"Dannemann Pierrot\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Mini format, 10 دقيقة. Vanilla or cherry flavoring. The Brazilian recreational cigar — convivial, unpretentious, festive. Smoked at Rio carnivals and football matches for 50 years.\", \"force\": \"Light\", \"wrapper\": \"Brazilian Bahia\", \"vitolas\": [\"Pierrot\", \"Pierrot Vanilla\", \"Pierrot Cherry\"]}, {\"name\": \"Dannemann Premium\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"The serious side of Dannemann — full-length cigars, 2-year-aged Bahia tobacco. More complex notes than the standard ranges: فانيليا, cashew, light قرفة spice. Robusto and Toro formats. The discovery for المتحمسون who knew Dannemann only from the cigarillos.\", \"force\": \"Light-Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Brazilian Bahia\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Toro\", \"Corona\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Gerhard Dannemann\", \"anecdote\": \"The German immigrant who discovered the qualities of Bahian tobacco where Brazilians themselves didn\'t yet value it. He is today commemorated by a statue in São Félix da Cachoeira — the only city in the world whose main monument represents a cigar maker.\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Gerhard Dannemann\", \"anecdote\": \"The German immigrant who discovered the qualities of Bahian tobacco where Brazilians themselves didn\'t yet value it. He is today commemorated by a statue in São Félix da Cachoeira — the only city in the world whose main monument represents a cigar maker.\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Gerhard Dannemann\", \"anecdote\": \"The German immigrant who discovered the qualities of Bahian tobacco where Brazilians themselves didn\'t yet value it. He is today commemorated by a statue in São Félix da Cachoeira — the only city in the world whose main monument represents a cigar maker.\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Gerhard Dannemann\", \"anecdote\": \"The German immigrant who discovered the qualities of Bahian tobacco where Brazilians themselves didn\'t yet value it. He is today commemorated by a statue in São Félix da Cachoeira — the only city 在世界上 whose main monument represents a cigar maker.\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Gerhard Dannemann\", \"anecdote\": \"The German immigrant who discovered the qualities of Bahian tobacco where Brazilians themselves didn\'t yet value it. He is today commemorated by a statue in São Félix da Cachoeira — the only city في العالم whose main monument represents a cigar maker.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Caipirinha\", \"name\": \"Classic Caipirinha\", \"notes\": \"The Brazilian national pairing — the sugarcane sweetness of caipirinha naturally embraces the sweet notes of Bahia tobacco. A beach, party, sunshine pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"Coffee\", \"name\": \"Brazilian coado coffee\", \"notes\": \"The filtered Brazilian coffee, light and gentle, has been the daily pairing of São Félix residents for 150 years.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\": \"Caipirinha\", \"name\": \"Classic Caipirinha\", \"notes\": \"The Brazilian national pairing — the sugarcane sweetness of caipirinha naturally embraces the sweet notas de Bahia tobacco. A beach, party, sunshine pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"Café\", \"name\": \"Brazilian coado coffee\", \"notes\": \"The filtered Brazilian coffee, light and gentle, has been the daily pairing of São Félix residents for 150 years.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\": \"Caipirinha\", \"name\": \"Classic Caipirinha\", \"notes\": \"The Brazilian national pairing — the sugarcane sweetness of caipirinha naturally embraces the sweet Noten von Bahia tobacco. A beach, party, sunshine pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"Kaffee\", \"name\": \"Brazilian coado coffee\", \"notes\": \"The filtered Brazilian coffee, light and gentle, has been the daily pairing of São Félix residents for 150 years.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\": \"Caipirinha\", \"name\": \"Classic Caipirinha\", \"notes\": \"The Brazilian national pairing — the sugarcane sweetness of caipirinha naturally embraces the sweet 风味： Bahia tobacco. A beach, party, sunshine pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"咖啡\", \"name\": \"Brazilian coado coffee\", \"notes\": \"The filtered Brazilian coffee, light and gentle, has been the daily pairing of São Félix residents for 150 years.\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\": \"Caipirinha\", \"name\": \"Classic Caipirinha\", \"notes\": \"The Brazilian national pairing — the sugarcane sweetness of caipirinha naturally embraces the sweet نكهات: Bahia tobacco. A beach, party, sunshine pairing.\"}, {\"type\": \"القهوة\", \"name\": \"Brazilian coado coffee\", \"notes\": \"The filtered Brazilian coffee, light and gentle, has been the daily pairing of São Félix residents for 150 years.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Dannemann';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'Zino Davidoff grew up behind a tobacco counter. His father Henrion had fled the Russian pogroms, arriving in Geneva in 1911 with the skills of a Kiev tobacco merchant and the immigrant\'s determination to make them count. The family shop on Rue de Rive became one of Geneva\'s most respected specialty tobacconists — a place where serious buyers sought serious guidance. Zino learned the trade from childhood and absorbed something more important: that tobacco expertise was meaningless without the ability to communicate it.\r\n\r\nIn 1968, he launched under his own name the range that would transform European cigar culture. His commercial genius was specific: he convinced the Cuban tobacco monopoly to produce exclusive blends bearing the Davidoff name, at price points and in packaging that explicitly positioned them above every other cigar in the world. \'Davidoff de La Havane\' became, for 22 years, the aspirational peak of cigar culture — the object of desire for anyone who understood what a cigar was supposed to be and was willing to pay accordingly.\r\n\r\nThe rupture of 1990 was the most dramatic event in modern cigar history. Davidoff had grown increasingly concerned about the consistency of Havana\'s production — leaves arriving that did not match specifications, cigars with draw problems, batches that varied unacceptably from one box to the next. After private negotiations failed to resolve the situation, Zino announced publicly that Davidoff was ending its Cuban relationship and transferring production to the Dominican Republic.\r\n\r\nThe cigar world was stunned. Vintage Cuban Davidoffs — already accumulated in cellars by collectors who sensed what was coming — became immediately valuable. They are today among the most prized collectibles in the secondary market, sold at specialist auctions at prices that reflect their status as the end of an era.\r\n\r\nDominican Davidoffs are different cigars. Softer, more floral, more immediately accessible than the Cuban originals, they represent the house\'s argument that Dominican tobacco, selected and blended with the same rigor that Zino applied to his Cuban relationships, can produce cigars of equivalent sophistication. The market has largely accepted that argument. The Davidoff Millennium Blend, the Signature, and the Year of the series consistently earn scores between 92 and 96 and maintain the brand\'s position at the apex of the accessible premium market.', `history_es` = 'Zino Davidoff lanzó en Ginebra en 1968 la gama que revolucionaría la percepción del cigarro en Europa. Convenció a Cuba de producir los exclusivos \'Davidoff de La Havane\' — los más caros del mundo durante 25 años. En 1990, tras una ruptura dramática con Habanos por problemas de calidad, trasladó la producción a República Dominicana. Los \'Davidoff cubanos\' vintage son hoy piezas de museo.', `history_de` = 'Zino Davidoff lancierte 1968 in Genf die Linie, die die europäische Wahrnehmung der Zigarre revolutionieren sollte. Er überzeugte Kuba, die exklusiven \'Davidoff de La Havane\' zu produzieren — 25 Jahre lang die teuersten Zigarren der Welt. 1990 verlegte er nach einem dramatischen Bruch mit Habanos die Produktion in die Dominikanische Republik. Vintage \'kubanische Davidoffs\' sind heute Museumsstücke.', `history_zh` = '齐诺·大卫杜夫于1968年在日内瓦推出了改变欧洲雪茄认知的产品线。他说服古巴生产独家的\'哈瓦那大卫杜夫\'——25年间全球最昂贵的雪茄。1990年与哈瓦那斯公司因质量问题戏剧性决裂后，他将生产转移至多米尼加共和国。古巴大卫杜夫老年份如今是博物馆藏品。', `history_ar` = 'زينو ديفيدوف أطلق عام 1968 في جنيف تشكيلته التي ستحدث ثورة في تصور السيجار الأوروبي. أقنع كوبا بإنتاج \'ديفيدوف دو لا هافان\' الحصريّة — الأغلى في العالم لمدة 25 عامًا. عام 1990، بعد قطيعة درامية مع هابانوس بسبب مشاكل الجودة، نقل الإنتاج إلى جمهورية الدومينيكان.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Signature Series\", \"color\": \"#C9A96E\", \"story\": \"The founding range — Anniversario No.1 and No.2, launched in Cuba in 1968. Since the Dominican transfer, these have become their own reference of finesse. Notes of white flowers, toasted grain, sandalwood. The incarnation of luxury without ostentation.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Dominican\", \"vitolas\": [\"Anniversario No.1\", \"Anniversario No.2\", \"2000\", \"3000\", \"4000\", \"5000\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 93, \"year\": 2021}]}, {\"name\": \"Winston Churchill\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"Launched in 2013, tribute to the greatest smoker of the 20th century. Official collaboration with the Churchill family. Bolder than the classic Davidoff range — a major stylistic shift. Notes of leather, smoky wood, oriental spices. The Late Hour is the nocturnal, even more intense version.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian Sun-Grown\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro\", \"Robusto\", \"Churchill\", \"The Original\", \"The Late Hour\", \"The Statesman\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 94, \"year\": 2022}]}, {\"name\": \"Nicaragua\", \"color\": \"#8B2500\", \"story\": \"Launched 2016, total stylistic break. Davidoff explores Nicaraguan tobacco — the boldest in its catalog. Notes of dark chocolate, coffee, tanned leather. The Nicaragua range proves the Geneva house can navigate all intensities without sacrificing its demand for consistency.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Nicaraguan\", \"vitolas\": [\"Box Pressed Toro\", \"Box Pressed Robusto\", \"Box Pressed Torpedo\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 95, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"Colorado\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Ecuadorian oscuro wrapper over Dominican. The middle range between Signature finesse and Nicaragua power. Notes of hazelnut, café au lait, light spices. The best-seller in European lounges — accessible, consistent, rewarding.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Churchill\", \"Toro\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Signature Series\", \"color\": \"#C9A96E\", \"story\": \"The founding range — Anniversario No.1 and No.2, launched in Cuba in 1968. Since the Dominican transfer, these have become their own reference of finesse. Notas de white flowers, tostado grain, sandalwood. The incarnation of luxury without ostentation.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Dominican\", \"vitolas\": [\"Anniversario No.1\", \"Anniversario No.2\", \"2000\", \"3000\", \"4000\", \"5000\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 93, \"year\": 2021}]}, {\"name\": \"Winston Churchill\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"Lanzada en 2013, tribute to the greatest smoker of the 20th century. Official collaboration with the Churchill family. Bolder than the classic Davidoff range — a major stylistic shift. Notas de cuero, smoky wood, oriental especias. The Late Hour is the nocturnal, even more intense version.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian Sun-Grown\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro\", \"Robusto\", \"Churchill\", \"The Original\", \"The Late Hour\", \"The Statesman\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 94, \"year\": 2022}]}, {\"name\": \"Nicaragua\", \"color\": \"#8B2500\", \"story\": \"Launched 2016, total stylistic break. Davidoff explores Nicaraguan tobacco — the boldest in its catalog. Notas de chocolate negro, café, tanned cuero. The Nicaragua range proves the Geneva house can navigate all intensities without sacrificing its demand for consistency.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Nicaraguan\", \"vitolas\": [\"Box Pressed Toro\", \"Box Pressed Robusto\", \"Box Pressed Torpedo\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 95, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"Colorado\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Ecuadorian oscuro wrapper over Dominican. The middle range between Signature finesse and Nicaragua power. Notas de avellana, café au lait, light especias. El más vendido en European lounges — accessible, consistent, rewarding.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Churchill\", \"Toro\"]}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Signature Series\", \"color\": \"#C9A96E\", \"story\": \"The founding range — Anniversario No.1 and No.2, launched in Cuba in 1968. Since the Dominican transfer, these have become their own reference of finesse. Noten von white flowers, geröstet grain, sandalwood. The incarnation of luxury without ostentation.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Dominican\", \"vitolas\": [\"Anniversario No.1\", \"Anniversario No.2\", \"2000\", \"3000\", \"4000\", \"5000\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 93, \"year\": 2021}]}, {\"name\": \"Winston Churchill\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"Lanciert 2013, tribute to the greatest smoker of the 20th century. Official collaboration with the Churchill family. Bolder than the classic Davidoff range — a major stylistic shift. Noten von Leder, smoky wood, oriental Gewürze. The Late Hour is the nocturnal, even more intense version.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Ecuadorian Sun-Grown\", \"vitolas\": [\"Toro\", \"Robusto\", \"Churchill\", \"The Original\", \"The Late Hour\", \"The Statesman\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 94, \"year\": 2022}]}, {\"name\": \"Nicaragua\", \"color\": \"#8B2500\", \"story\": \"Launched 2016, total stylistic break. Davidoff explores Nicaraguan tobacco — the boldest in its catalog. Noten von dunkle Schokolade, Kaffee, tanned Leder. The Nicaragua range proves the Geneva house can navigate all intensities without sacrificing its demand for consistency.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Nicaraguan\", \"vitolas\": [\"Box Pressed Toro\", \"Box Pressed Robusto\", \"Box Pressed Torpedo\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 95, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"Colorado\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Ecuadorian oscuro wrapper over Dominican. The middle range between Signature finesse and Nicara