in every puff.\", \"force\": \"Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Oscuro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Revolution\", \"Presidente\"]}, {\"name\": \"Te Amo Natural\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Natural San Andrés wrapper (non-maduro) over Dominican-Mexican. نكهات:  بندق, dried herbs, light spice. Accessible Medium. The range for discovering Te Amo without the Maduro commitment.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Mexican San Andrés Natural\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robusto\", \"Churchill\", \"Toro\"]}]', `celebrities_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Aztecs and Totonacs\", \"anecdote\": \"San Andrés Tuxtla tobacco was used in Aztec religious ceremonies — offered to the gods during ritual sacrifices. Te Amo cultivates the same soil, in the same valley, with the same patience as pre-Columbian cultivators. Mexican Maduro wrapper is one of the few direct links between pre-Columbian civilization and the modern cigar.\"}]', `celebrities_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Aztecs and Totonacs\", \"anecdote\": \"San Andrés Tuxtla tobacco was used in Aztec religious ceremonies — offered to the gods during ritual sacrifices. Te Amo cultivates the same soil, in the same valley, with the same patience as pre-Columbian cultivators. Mexican Maduro wrapper is one of the few direct links between pre-Columbian civilization and the modern cigar.\"}]', `celebrities_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Aztecs and Totonacs\", \"anecdote\": \"San Andrés Tuxtla tobacco was used in Aztec religious ceremonies — offered to the gods during ritual sacrifices. Te Amo cultivates the same soil, in the same valley, with the same patience as pre-Columbian cultivators. Mexican Maduro wrapper is one of the few direct links between pre-Columbian civilization and the modern cigar.\"}]', `celebrities_zh` = '[{\"name\": \"Aztecs and Totonacs\", \"anecdote\": \"San Andrés Tuxtla tobacco was used in Aztec religious ceremonies — offered to the gods during ritual sacrifices. Te Amo cultivates the same soil, in the same valley, with the same patience as pre-Columbian cultivators. Mexican Maduro wrapper is one of the few direct links between pre-Columbian civilization and the modern cigar.\"}]', `celebrities_ar` = '[{\"name\": \"Aztecs and Totonacs\", \"anecdote\": \"San Andrés Tuxtla tobacco was used in Aztec religious ceremonies — offered to the gods during ritual sacrifices. Te Amo cultivates the same soil, in the same valley, with the same patience as pre-Columbian cultivators. Mexican Maduro wrapper is one of the few direct links between pre-Columbian civilization and the modern cigar.\"}]', `pairings_en` = '[{\"type\": \"Mezcal\", \"name\": \"Artisanal Oaxacan mezcal\", \"notes\": \"Two exceptional Mexican products — the maguey mezcal and the volcanic Veracruz tobacco. Shared earthy notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"Coffee\", \"name\": \"Veracruz coffee\", \"notes\": \"The coffee from the same region as the tobacco — shared chocolaty notes of both Veracruz mountain terroirs.\"}]', `pairings_es` = '[{\"type\": \"Mezcal\", \"name\": \"Artisanal Oaxacan mezcal\", \"notes\": \"Two exceptional Mexican products — the maguey mezcal and the volcanic Veracruz tobacco. Shared earthy notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"Café\", \"name\": \"Veracruz coffee\", \"notes\": \"The coffee from the same region as the tobacco — shared chocolaty notas de both Veracruz mountain terroirs.\"}]', `pairings_de` = '[{\"type\": \"Mezcal\", \"name\": \"Artisanal Oaxacan mezcal\", \"notes\": \"Two exceptional Mexican products — the maguey mezcal and the volcanic Veracruz tobacco. Shared earthy notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"Kaffee\", \"name\": \"Veracruz coffee\", \"notes\": \"The coffee from the same region as the tobacco — shared chocolaty Noten von both Veracruz mountain terroirs.\"}]', `pairings_zh` = '[{\"type\": \"Mezcal\", \"name\": \"Artisanal Oaxacan mezcal\", \"notes\": \"Two exceptional Mexican products — the maguey mezcal and the volcanic Veracruz tobacco. Shared earthy notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"咖啡\", \"name\": \"Veracruz coffee\", \"notes\": \"The coffee from the same region as the tobacco — shared chocolaty 风味： both Veracruz mountain terroirs.\"}]', `pairings_ar` = '[{\"type\": \"Mezcal\", \"name\": \"Artisanal Oaxacan mezcal\", \"notes\": \"Two exceptional Mexican products — the maguey mezcal and the volcanic Veracruz tobacco. Shared earthy notes.\"}, {\"type\": \"القهوة\", \"name\": \"Veracruz coffee\", \"notes\": \"The coffee from the same region as the tobacco — shared chocolaty نكهات: both Veracruz mountain terroirs.\"}]' WHERE `name` = 'Te Amo';
UPDATE `brands` SET `history_en` = 'Trinidad\'s story begins in the most rarefied space in Cuban politics: the personal gift list of Fidel Castro. In 1969, three years after Cohiba was created for Castro\'s own use, a second ultra-premium brand was commissioned for a different purpose — not personal consumption but state diplomacy of the highest order. The brief was precise: a cigar so exceptional that giving it to a head of state would be understood immediately as a gesture of extraordinary esteem. A cigar, in other words, that could not be bought.\r\n\r\nFor 29 years, Trinidad was precisely that. It existed in the cellars of the Cuban foreign ministry and the luggage of diplomatic delegations. It circulated among the heads of the Non-Aligned Movement, the leaders of newly independent African nations, selected European statesmen. Nelson Mandela received it. So did several African heads of state whose support Cuba was courting. So, reportedly, did various figures in European and Latin American politics whose names have never been officially confirmed. Trinidad was statecraft in cedar and tobacco.\r\n\r\nThe format chosen for this period was the Fundadores: 40 x 192mm, the longest Cuban cigar ever produced at commercial scale. Nearly 20 centimeters of pure Vuelta Abajo — a single continuous smoking experience that can last two hours and passes through aromatic phases as distinct as acts in a play. The thinness of the ring gauge produces a cooler, more concentrated draw that amplifies the subtlety of the tobacco rather than its power. It is a cigar that requires full attention and rewards it completely.\r\n\r\nThe public unveiling came in November 1998, at a gala dinner organized by Davidoff in Paris. The announcement that Trinidad would finally be available commercially caused a sensation in the cigar world disproportionate to any marketing campaign. Here was a brand that enthusiasts had been hearing rumors about for three decades — and in some cases had tasted in private, passed along by contacts in diplomatic circles — suddenly placed on the market. The Fundadores sold out immediately and has remained chronically undersupplied ever since.\r\n\r\nTrinidad\'s production remains the smallest of any major Cuban house. The factory allocates a fraction of its capacity to Trinidad, using tobaccos that go through the same rigorous leaf selection process as Cohiba — the closest comparison in the portfolio. The Reyes, a Petit Corona added to the line in 2003, made the brand accessible in a shorter format while preserving the house profile: refined, complex, surprisingly strong for its apparent elegance. The Coloniales, a Corona Extra, sits between the two in both size and character.\r\n\r\nThe brand\'s mystique has not diminished with commercial availability. If anything, the knowledge that Trinidad spent its first three decades as a diplomatic secret has deepened the devotion of its collectors. These are not smokers who came to Trinidad because they saw it reviewed. They came because someone who had been somewhere extraordinary told them, quietly, what they had smoked.', `history_es` = 'Trinidad fue creada en 1969 como regalo diplomático de Estado, igual que Cohiba. Durante 29 años sólo existió en los maletines de los ministros cubanos. En 1998, se lanzó públicamente en una gala de Davidoff en París — con el Fundadores (40x192mm), el cigarro cubano comercial más largo jamás producido. La marca más rara y misteriosa de Cuba.', `history_de` = 'Trinidad wurde 1969 als staatliches diplomatisches Geschenk geschaffen, genau wie Cohiba. Achtundzwanzig Jahre lang existierte sie nur in den Aktentaschen kubanischer Minister. 1998 wurde sie bei einer Davidoff-Gala in Paris öffentlich vorgestellt — mit dem Fundadores (40x192mm), der längsten je produzierten kubanischen Zigarre.', `history_zh` = '特立尼达于1969年作为国家外交礼物创立，与科伊巴一样。29年间它只存在于古巴部长们的公文包里。1998年在大卫杜夫巴黎晚宴上公开发布——推出了Fundadores（40×192mm），有史以来商业生产的最长古巴雪茄。古巴最稀有、最神秘的品牌。', `history_ar` = 'أُنشئت ترينيداد عام 1969 هدية دبلوماسية من الدولة، شأنها شأن كوهيبا. ظلت 29 عامًا حكرًا على حقائب الوزراء الكوبيين. عام 1998 أُطلقت علنًا في حفل ديفيدوف بباريس — مع فوندادوريس (40×192ملم)، أطول سيجار كوبي تجاري أُنتج على الإطلاق. أندر وأغمض علامة كوبية.', `gamme_en` = '[{\"name\": \"Fundadores\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The original format — Laguito No.1 (40 x 192mm), 120 minutes of smoke. One of the longest cigars ever commercialized. Its extreme thinness (ring gauge 40) makes it a demanding cigar: it must be smoked slowly, in windless conditions. Notes of fresh cedar, white flowers, rock honey.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Fundadores\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 95, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"Reyes\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Petit Corona (40 x 110mm). Trinidad\'s short range — accessible, floral, sweet. The Reyes is often considered the best \'small Cuban cigar.\' In 20 minutes, it delivers all the floral and creamy complexity of the house without requiring a Fundadores.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Reyes\"]}, {\"name\": \"Coloniales\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"Petit Edmundo format (52 x 110mm). The only wide Trinidad vitola — it reveals a bolder, spicier profile than the house\'s thin formats. Notes of cinnamon, ebony, coffee. A surprise for Fundadores enthusiasts discovering a Trinidad at the opposite end.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Coloniales\"]}, {\"name\": \"Robustos Extra\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Robusto Extra (50 x 155mm). The premium vitola of the modern range. Maximum house complexity in a 60-minute format. Limited edition, produced in minuscule quantities. Connoisseurs queue at each launch.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robustos Extra\"]}]', `gamme_es` = '[{\"name\": \"Fundadores\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The original format — Laguito No.1 (40 x 192mm), 120 minutes of smoke. One of the longest cigars ever commercialized. Its extreme thinness (ring gauge 40) makes it a demanding cigar: it must be smoked slowly, in windless conditions. Notas de fresh cedro, white flowers, rock miel.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Fundadores\"], \"scores\": [{\"source\": \"Cigar Aficionado\", \"score\": 95, \"year\": 2020}]}, {\"name\": \"Reyes\", \"color\": \"#A0522D\", \"story\": \"Petit Corona (40 x 110mm). Trinidad\'s short range — accessible, floral, sweet. The Reyes is often considerado the best \'small Cuban cigar.\' In 20 minutes, it ofrece all the floral and creamy complexity of the house without requiring a Fundadores.\", \"force\": \"Medium\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Claro\", \"vitolas\": [\"Reyes\"]}, {\"name\": \"Coloniales\", \"color\": \"#8B4513\", \"story\": \"Petit Edmundo format (52 x 110mm). The only wide Trinidad vitola — it revela a bolder, spicier profile than la thin formats. Notas de canela, ebony, café. A surprise for Fundadores aficionados discovering a Trinidad at the opposite end.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Coloniales\"]}, {\"name\": \"Robustos Extra\", \"color\": \"#722F37\", \"story\": \"Robusto Extra (50 x 155mm). The premium vitola of the modern range. Maximum house complexity in a 60-minute format. Limited edition, produced in minuscule quantities. Connoisseurs queue at each launch.\", \"force\": \"Medium-Full\", \"wrapper\": \"Habano Colorado\", \"vitolas\": [\"Robustos Extra\"]}]', `gamme_de` = '[{\"name\": \"Fundadores\", \"color\": \"#8B6914\", \"story\": \"The original format — Laguito No.1 (40 x 192mm), 120 minutes of smoke. One of the longest cigars ever commercialized. Its extreme thinness (ring gauge 40) makes it a demanding cigar: it must be smoked slowly, in windless conditions. Noten von fresh Zeder, white flowers, r